{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CgdCaNuJzYBXZqhMeMLGH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01L8xuhMRHfyzAyYKbzRa1r3","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/al/dev/MOSP/reports/scratch/edwards_mcdermid/02_lemmas/check.py","content":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Brute-force check of every intermediate statement of the Edwards–McDermid\nchain (loop0012 item 02; `reports/edwards_mcdermid.md` §2; the plan is\n`reports/edwards_mcdermid_plan.md` §0.3–0.5) on every graph on 1–9 vertices\nfrom `nauty-geng`, pathwidth by the vertex-separation subset DP.\n\nThe statements, numbered as in the report's §2 (W = weights, C = cut lemma,\nP = potential, R = reduction system, S = step inequality, T = Theorem 3.2,\nA = assembly budgets, B = basic graphs, H = the shape of hypothesis (H3)):\n\n  W1–W5  recurrence, g non-decreasing, g' non-increasing from 3, property 6,\n         0 ≤ g < 1 and 0 ≤ g' ≤ 1/6, the closed form (exact rationals, to n = 40;\n         main process)\n  C1     pw(G) ≤ max(pw(G[V1]) + |∂1|, pw(G[V2]) + |∂2|, |∂1| + |∂2| − 1)\n         (every partition to 7 vertices; sampled partitions at 8–9); C1s is the\n         same without the middle term, measured only\n  C2     iterated form on a depth-2 bisection: pw(G) ≤ 2 Σ_i b_i + max_leaf pw\n  P1     f(G − w) = f(G) − g(d(w)) − Σ_{v ∈ N(w)} g'(d(v))        (every w)\n  P2     degrees 0 or ≥ 3, w of maximum degree Δ ≥ 4 with a neighbour of degree\n         ≤ Δ − 1 ⇒ f(G − w) ≤ f(G) − 1; Δ-regular, Δ ≥ 4 ⇒\n         f(G − w) = f(G) − 1 + g'(Δ − 1) − g'(Δ)\n  R1     every SPStep (at a vertex of degree 1 or 2) removes ≥ 1 edge\n  R2     every SPStep lowers no degree-count: deg_{H'}(u) ≤ deg_H(u) for all u,\n         hence f(H') ≤ f(H); a vertex of degree d isolated by the step loses g(d)\n  R3     commutation: SPStep H H' at v, w ≠ v ⇒ H' − w = H − w, or\n         H' − w = SPStep (H − w) at v (with v of degree 1 or 2 in H − w)\n  R5     a step at v inside a component acts on that component only\n  R6     one step costs at most one: pw(H) ≤ pw(H') + 1 (sampled at 9)\n  RU     (measured) every maximal reduction order reaches the same reduct\n  S0     the hinge: G* a reduced reduct of G' = G − w, v with d_{G'}(v) = d ≥ 3\n         ⇒ f(G') − f(G*) + g'(δ(G*)) ≥ g'(d)\n  S1     the step inequality for the paper's choice of w; S1′ for every\n         maximum-degree w (measured); both in the global-minimum form\n         1 + f(G*) − g'(δ(G*)) ≤ f(G) − g'(δ(G)), which implies the\n         per-component form 1 + f⁻(G*) ≤ f⁻(G)\n  SJ     the j-identity (paper (2)–(4)): 1 + f(G') = f(G) − j1 − j2 − j3\n  T1     Algorithm X: X, B with B non-empty, reduced, basic,\n         |X| + f⁻(B) ≤ f⁻(G); and (measured) r(G − X) = B\n  A1/A2  the budgets the record needs at n ≤ 9: max of pw − f⁻ over reduced\n         graphs and of pw − main term over all graphs, per n\n  B1     connected, every degree ≥ 3, not cubic ⇒ f⁻ ≥ 5/6; connected cubic ⇒\n         f⁻ = N/6 − 1/6; f⁻(component) ≥ 0; additivity over components\n  H3     pw(G) − pw(r(G)) per n (its maximum is the shape of (H3) at these sizes)\n\nA violation prints the graph6 string and stops (unless --no-stop).\n\n    nice -n 19 python3 reports/scratch/edwards_mcdermid/02_lemmas/check.py --max-n 9 --workers 8\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport collections\nimport json\nimport random\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nimport time\nfrom fractions import Fraction\nfrom multiprocessing import Pool\n\nsys.path.insert(0, \"/home/al/dev/MOSP\")\n\nfrom learning.edwards_mcdermid import (  # noqa: E402\n    alternating_factorial, bits, components, degrees, edge_count, f_potential,\n    fminus, g, g_closed_form, g_prime, is_cubic, is_reduced, min_degree, reduce,\n)\n\nHERE = \"/home/al/dev/MOSP/reports/scratch/edwards_mcdermid/02_lemmas\"\n\n# sampling at 8–9 vertices (the exhaustive partition sweep is 2^(n−1) DPs per\n# graph and does not fit the budget there; see the report)\nC1_PARTITIONS = 32      # random partitions per sampled graph at n = 8, 9\nC2_TREES = 4            # random depth-2 bisection trees per sampled graph\nSAMPLE_STRIDE_9 = 8     # at n = 9 the pathwidth-heavy checks run on every 8th graph\nRANDOM_ORDERS = {8: 200, 9: 60}   # reduction orders per graph for RU (200 below 8)\nS1_RANDOM_REDUCTS = 5   # random reducts of G − w for S1 beside the canonical one\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# graphs\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\ndef parse_g6(line: str) -> tuple[int, list[int]]:\n    b = line.strip().encode()\n    n = b[0] - 63\n    bitlist: list[int] = []\n    for ch in b[1:]:\n        v = ch - 63\n        bitlist += [(v >> i) & 1 for i in range(5, -1, -1)]\n    adj = [0] * n\n    k = 0\n    for j in range(1, n):\n        for i in range(j):\n            if bitlist[k]:\n                adj[i] |= 1 << j\n                adj[j] |= 1 << i\n            k += 1\n    return n, adj\n\n\ndef pw_induced(adj: list[int], S: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Vertex separation (= pathwidth) of G[S], by the subset DP over the\n    submasks of S in increasing numeric order.\"\"\"\n    if S == 0:\n        return 0\n    f = {0: 0}\n    T = (0 - S) & S\n    while True:\n        rest = S & ~T\n        cost = 0\n        U = T\n        while U:\n            low = U & -U\n            U ^= low\n            if adj[low.bit_length() - 1] & rest:\n                cost += 1\n        best = None\n        U = T\n        while U:\n            low = U & -U\n            U ^= low\n            c = f[T ^ low]\n            if best is None or c < best:\n                best = c\n        f[T] = cost if cost > best else best\n        if T == S:\n            break\n        T = (T - S) & S\n    return f[S]\n\n\ndef support(adj: list[int]) -> int:\n    m = 0\n    for v, a in enumerate(adj):\n        if a:\n            m |= 1 << v\n    return m\n\n\ndef isolate(adj: list[int], w: int) -> list[int]:\n    out = list(adj)\n    for u in bits(adj[w]):\n        out[u] &= ~(1 << w)\n    out[w] = 0\n    return out\n\n\ndef isolate_set(adj: list[int], X: int) -> list[int]:\n    out = list(adj)\n    for w in bits(X):\n        out = isolate(out, w)\n    return out\n\n\ndef sp_step(adj: list[int], v: int) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"One series-parallel operation at `v`, which must have degree 1 or 2.\"\"\"\n    d = adj[v].bit_count()\n    assert d in (1, 2), d\n    nb = adj[v]\n    out = isolate(adj, v)\n    if d == 2:\n        low = nb & -nb\n        x = low.bit_length() - 1\n        y = (nb ^ low).bit_length() - 1\n        if not (adj[x] >> y) & 1:\n            out[x] |= 1 << y\n            out[y] |= 1 << x\n    return out\n\n\ndef step_vertices(adj: list[int]) -> list[int]:\n    return [v for v in range(len(adj)) if 1 <= adj[v].bit_count() <= 2]\n\n\ndef reduce_random(adj: list[int], rng: random.Random) -> list[int]:\n    adj = list(adj)\n    while True:\n        cands = step_vertices(adj)\n        if not cands:\n            return adj\n        adj = sp_step(adj, rng.choice(cands))\n\n\ndef connected_on_support(adj: list[int]) -> bool:\n    return len(components(adj)) == 1\n\n\ndef is_empty(adj: list[int]) -> bool:\n    return not any(adj)\n\n\ndef global_min_degree(adj: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"δ over the support; 0 for the empty graph.\"\"\"\n    s = support(adj)\n    return min_degree(adj, s) if s else 0\n\n\ndef F_global(adj: list[int]) -> Fraction:\n    \"\"\"f(H) − g'(δ(H)) with δ over the support (the paper's one-component f⁻).\"\"\"\n    return f_potential(adj) - g_prime(global_min_degree(adj))\n\n\ndef restrict(adj: list[int], C: int) -> list[int]:\n    return [adj[v] & C if (C >> v) & 1 else 0 for v in range(len(adj))]\n\n\ndef is_basic_component(adj: list[int], C: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"`adj` restricted to its component `C` (every degree ≥ 3 there): cubic,\n    or some v ∈ C with r(G|C − v) empty.\"\"\"\n    sub = restrict(adj, C)\n    if is_cubic(sub, C):\n        return True\n    for v in bits(C):\n        radj, _ = reduce(isolate(sub, v))\n        if is_empty(radj):\n            return True\n    return False\n\n\ndef is_basic(adj: list[int]) -> bool:\n    return all(is_basic_component(adj, C) for C in components(adj))\n\n\ndef paper_choice(adj: list[int], C: int | None = None) -> tuple[list[int], list[int], int]:\n    \"\"\"Maximum-degree vertices (within `C` if given), those among them whose\n    lowest-degree neighbour has the smallest degree (the paper's rule), and Δ.\"\"\"\n    verts = list(bits(C)) if C is not None else [v for v in range(len(adj)) if adj[v]]\n    deg = degrees(adj)\n    Delta = max(deg[v] for v in verts)\n    maxs = [v for v in verts if deg[v] == Delta]\n    key = {v: min(deg[u] for u in bits(adj[v])) for v in maxs}\n    best = min(key.values())\n    return maxs, [v for v in maxs if key[v] == best], Delta\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# the per-graph worker\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\ndef one(args: tuple[int, str]) -> dict:\n    idx, line = args\n    n, adj = parse_g6(line)\n    rng = random.Random(idx * 1_000_003 + n)\n    cnt: collections.Counter = collections.Counter()\n    mx: dict[str, Fraction | int] = {}\n    viol: list[str] = []\n\n    def bump(key: str, value):\n        if key not in mx or value > mx[key]:\n            mx[key] = value\n\n    def bad(stmt: str, detail: str):\n        viol.append(f\"{stmt}\\t{line.strip()}\\t{detail}\")\n\n    deg = degrees(adj)\n    full = (1 << n) - 1\n    supp = support(adj)\n    heavy = n < 9 or idx % SAMPLE_STRIDE_9 == 0\n\n    # pathwidth of G and of r(G)\n    pw = pw_induced(adj, full)\n    radj, removed = reduce(adj)\n    pw_r = pw_induced(radj, support(radj))\n    cnt[\"graphs\"] += 1\n    gap = pw - pw_r\n    if gap < 0:\n        bad(\"H3-minor\", f\"pw={pw} pw_r={pw_r}\")\n    bump(\"H3_gap\", gap)\n    cnt[f\"H3_gap_{gap}\"] += 1\n    main_term = f_potential(radj)\n    bump(\"A2_pw_minus_main\", pw - main_term)\n    reduced = is_reduced(adj)\n    if reduced:\n        cnt[\"reduced\"] += 1\n        bump(\"A1_pw_minus_fminus\", pw - fminus(adj))\n        if gap != 0:\n            bad(\"H3-reduced\", \"a reduced graph is its own reduct\")\n\n    # ---- P1, P2: one deletion -------------------------------------------\n    f_G = f_potential(adj)\n    Delta = max(deg) if n else 0\n    for w in range(n):\n        Gw = isolate(adj, w)\n        lhs = f_potential(Gw)\n        rhs = f_G - g(deg[w]) - sum((g_prime(deg[v]) for v in bits(adj[w])), Fraction(0))\n        cnt[\"P1\"] += 1\n        if lhs != rhs:\n            bad(\"P1\", f\"w={w} lhs={lhs} rhs={rhs}\")\n        if reduced and deg[w] == Delta and Delta >= 4:\n            if any(deg[v] <= Delta - 1 for v in bits(adj[w])):\n                cnt[\"P2\"] += 1\n                if not lhs <= f_G - 1:\n                    bad(\"P2\", f\"w={w} f(G-w)={lhs} f(G)={f_G}\")\n            if all(deg[v] == Delta for v in range(n) if adj[v]):\n                cnt[\"P2reg\"] += 1\n                if lhs != f_G - 1 + g_prime(Delta - 1) - g_prime(Delta):\n                    bad(\"P2reg\", f\"w={w} f(G-w)={lhs} f(G)={f_G} Delta={Delta}\")\n\n    # ---- R1, R2, R3, R5, R6: one step ----------------------------------\n    steps = step_vertices(adj)\n    comps = components(adj)\n    comp_of = {}\n    for C in comps:\n        for v in bits(C):\n            comp_of[v] = C\n    m_G = edge_count(adj)\n    for v in steps:\n        H2 = sp_step(adj, v)\n        cnt[\"R1\"] += 1\n        if not edge_count(H2) <= m_G - 1:\n            bad(\"R1\", f\"v={v}\")\n        d2 = degrees(H2)\n        cnt[\"R2\"] += 1\n        if any(d2[u] > deg[u] for u in range(n)):\n            bad(\"R2\", f\"v={v} degree rose\")\n        if not f_potential(H2) <= f_G:\n            bad(\"R2f\", f\"v={v}\")\n        if not f_G - f_potential(H2) >= g(deg[v]):\n            bad(\"R2iso\", f\"v={v}\")\n        # R3\n        for w in range(n):\n            if w == v:\n                continue\n            cnt[\"R3\"] += 1\n            Hw = isolate(adj, w)\n            H2w = isolate(H2, w)\n            if H2w == Hw:\n                cnt[\"R3_zero\"] += 1\n            elif 1 <= Hw[v].bit_count() <= 2 and sp_step(Hw, v) == H2w:\n                cnt[\"R3_one\"] += 1\n            else:\n                bad(\"R3\", f\"v={v} w={w}\")\n        # R5\n        if len(comps) >= 2:\n            C = comp_of[v]\n            cnt[\"R5\"] += 1\n            inside = restrict(adj, C)\n            outside = [adj[u] & ~C for u in range(n)]\n            lifted = sp_step(inside, v)\n            if [lifted[u] | outside[u] for u in range(n)] != H2:\n                bad(\"R5\", f\"v={v}\")\n        # R6 (pathwidth-heavy, sampled at 9)\n        if heavy:\n            cnt[\"R6\"] += 1\n            pw2 = pw_induced(H2, support(H2))\n            if not pw <= pw2 + 1:\n                bad(\"R6\", f\"v={v} pw={pw} pw'={pw2}\")\n            bump(\"R6_drop\", pw - pw2)\n\n    # ---- RU: uniqueness of the reduct -----------------------------------\n    if steps:\n        k = RANDOM_ORDERS.get(n, 200)\n        same = True\n        for _ in range(k):\n            if reduce_random(adj, rng) != radj:\n                same = False\n                break\n        cnt[\"RU_graphs\"] += 1\n        cnt[\"RU_orders\"] += k\n        if not same:\n            cnt[\"RU_nonunique\"] += 1\n\n    # ---- B1, additivity -------------------------------------------------\n    fm = fminus(adj)\n    tot = Fraction(0)\n    for C in comps:\n        sub = restrict(adj, C)\n        fc = fminus(sub)\n        tot += fc\n        cnt[\"B1_nonneg\"] += 1\n        if fc < 0:\n            bad(\"B1neg\", f\"component {C:b} fminus={fc}\")\n    cnt[\"B1_add\"] += 1\n    if tot != fm:\n        bad(\"B1add\", f\"sum={tot} fminus={fm}\")\n    connected = len(comps) == 1\n    min3 = bool(supp) and all(d == 0 or d >= 3 for d in deg)\n    if connected and min3:\n        if is_cubic(adj, supp):\n            N = supp.bit_count()\n            cnt[\"B1_cubic\"] += 1\n            if fm != Fraction(N, 6) - Fraction(1, 6):\n                bad(\"B1cubic\", f\"fminus={fm} N={N}\")\n        else:\n            cnt[\"B1_noncubic\"] += 1\n            if fm < Fraction(5, 6):\n                bad(\"B1floor\", f\"fminus={fm}\")\n\n    # ---- S0, S1, S1′, SJ: the step ----------------------------------------\n    if connected and min3:\n        basic = is_basic(adj)\n        cnt[\"S_conn_min3\"] += 1\n        if basic:\n            cnt[\"S_basic\"] += 1\n        else:\n            cnt[\"S_nonbasic\"] += 1\n            maxs, chosen, D = paper_choice(adj)\n            assert D >= 4\n            FG = F_global(adj)\n            for w in maxs:\n                Gp = isolate(adj, w)\n                dp = degrees(Gp)\n                reducts = [reduce(Gp)[0]]\n                for _ in range(S1_RANDOM_REDUCTS):\n                    r = reduce_random(Gp, rng)\n                    if r not in reducts:\n                        reducts.append(r)\n                nbrs = sorted(bits(adj[w]), key=lambda v: deg[v])\n                j1 = g_prime(deg[nbrs[0]]) - g_prime(D - 1)\n                j2 = g_prime(deg[nbrs[1]]) - g_prime(D)\n                j3 = sum((g_prime(deg[v]) - g_prime(D) for v in nbrs[2:]), Fraction(0))\n                cnt[\"SJ\"] += 1\n                if 1 + f_potential(Gp) != f_G - j1 - j2 - j3:\n                    bad(\"SJ\", f\"w={w}\")\n                for Gs in reducts:\n                    if is_empty(Gs):\n                        bad(\"S-empty\", f\"w={w}: G* empty though G is not basic\")\n                        continue\n                    f_Gs = f_potential(Gs)\n                    gd = g_prime(global_min_degree(Gs))\n                    # S0 for every v of degree ≥ 3 in G'\n                    for v in range(n):\n                        if dp[v] >= 3:\n                            cnt[\"S0\"] += 1\n                            if not f_potential(Gp) - f_Gs + gd >= g_prime(dp[v]):\n                                bad(\"S0\", f\"w={w} v={v}\")\n                    ok = 1 + f_Gs - gd <= FG\n                    okc = 1 + fminus(Gs) <= fm\n                    if w in chosen:\n                        cnt[\"S1\"] += 1\n                        if not ok:\n                            bad(\"S1\", f\"w={w} 1+F(G*)={1 + f_Gs - gd} F(G)={FG}\")\n                        if not okc:\n                            bad(\"S1c\", f\"w={w}\")\n                    cnt[\"S1p\"] += 1\n                    if not ok:\n                        cnt[\"S1p_fail\"] += 1\n                        if cnt[\"S1p_fail\"] == 1:\n                            cnt[\"S1p_first\"] = 0\n                            viol.append(f\"S1p-MEASURED\\t{line.strip()}\\tw={w} 1+F(G*)={1 + f_Gs - gd} F(G)={FG}\")\n                    if not okc:\n                        cnt[\"S1pc_fail\"] += 1\n\n    # ---- T1: Algorithm X -------------------------------------------------\n    if reduced and supp:\n        cnt[\"T1\"] += 1\n        X = 0\n        cur = list(adj)\n        while True:\n            comps_cur = components(cur)\n            nonbasic = [C for C in comps_cur if not is_basic_component(cur, C)]\n            if not nonbasic:\n                break\n            C = nonbasic[0]\n            _, chosen, _ = paper_choice(cur, C)\n            w = rng.choice(chosen)\n            X |= 1 << w\n            cur, _ = reduce(isolate(cur, w))\n        B = cur\n        if is_empty(B):\n            bad(\"T1empty\", f\"X={X:b}\")\n        if not is_reduced(B):\n            bad(\"T1reduced\", f\"X={X:b}\")\n        if not is_basic(B):\n            bad(\"T1basic\", f\"X={X:b}\")\n        if not X.bit_count() + fminus(B) <= fm:\n            bad(\"T1\", f\"X={X:b} |X|+fminus(B)={X.bit_count() + fminus(B)} fminus(G)={fm}\")\n        if X & ~supp:\n            bad(\"T1supp\", f\"X={X:b}\")\n        direct, _ = reduce(isolate_set(adj, X))\n        cnt[\"T1_direct\"] += 1\n        if direct != B:\n            cnt[\"T1_direct_differs\"] += 1\n        bump(\"T1_X\", X.bit_count())\n\n    # ---- C1, C2: the cut lemma --------------------------------------------\n    if heavy:\n        if n <= 7:\n            parts = range(0, 1 << (n - 1))     # V1 ∌ vertex n−1: each partition once\n        else:\n            parts = [rng.randrange(0, 1 << (n - 1)) for _ in range(C1_PARTITIONS)]\n        pwcache: dict[int, int] = {full: pw, 0: 0}\n\n        def pwS(S: int) -> int:\n            if S not in pwcache:\n                pwcache[S] = pw_induced(adj, S)\n            return pwcache[S]\n\n        for V1 in parts:\n            V2 = full & ~V1\n            b1 = sum(1 for v in bits(V1) if adj[v] & V2)\n            b2 = sum(1 for v in bits(V2) if adj[v] & V1)\n            bound = max(pwS(V1) + b1, pwS(V2) + b2, b1 + b2 - 1)\n            cnt[\"C1\"] += 1\n            if not pw <= bound:\n                bad(\"C1\", f\"V1={V1:b} pw={pw} bound={bound}\")\n            if pw <= max(pwS(V1) + b1, pwS(V2) + b2):\n                cnt[\"C1s_holds\"] += 1\n            bump(\"C1_slack\", bound - pw)\n        # C2: depth-2 bisection trees (random), budgets b_i = max boundary at level i\n        if n >= 4:\n            for _ in range(C2_TREES):\n                V1 = rng.randrange(0, 1 << (n - 1))\n                V2 = full & ~V1\n                lvl1 = max(sum(1 for v in bits(V1) if adj[v] & V2),\n                           sum(1 for v in bits(V2) if adj[v] & V1))\n                lvl2 = 0\n                leaves = []\n                for P in (V1, V2):\n                    pb = list(bits(P))\n                    sub = 0\n                    for v in pb:\n                        if rng.random() < 0.5:\n                            sub |= 1 << v\n                    Q1, Q2 = sub, P & ~sub\n                    lvl2 = max(lvl2,\n                               sum(1 for v in bits(Q1) if adj[v] & Q2),\n                               sum(1 for v in bits(Q2) if adj[v] & Q1))\n                    leaves += [pwS(Q1), pwS(Q2)]\n                bound = 2 * (lvl1 + lvl2) + max(leaves)\n                cnt[\"C2\"] += 1\n                if not pw <= bound:\n                    bad(\"C2\", f\"pw={pw} bound={bound}\")\n\n    return {\"n\": n, \"cnt\": cnt, \"mx\": mx, \"viol\": viol}\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# W1–W5 (main process)\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\ndef check_weights(N: int = 40) -> list[str]:\n    out = []\n    for d in range(4, N + 1):\n        assert d * g(d) == (d - 2) * g(d - 1) + g(d - 2) + 1, d          # W1\n    for d in range(0, N):\n        assert g(d + 1) >= g(d), d                                       # W2 (Lemma 8.3)\n    for d in range(3, N):\n        assert g_prime(d + 1) <= g_prime(d), d                           # W3 (Lemma 8.4)\n    for d in range(4, N + 1):\n        assert 1 - g(d) == (d - 1) * g_prime(d) + g_prime(d - 1), d      # W4 (property 6)\n    for d in range(0, N + 1):\n        assert 0 <= g(d) < 1, d                                          # W5a\n        assert 0 <= g_prime(d) <= Fraction(1, 6), d                      # W5b\n    for d in range(2, N + 1):\n        assert g_closed_form(d) == g(d), d                               # W5c (Lemma 8.1)\n    for d in range(5, N):                                                # property 5 (not used)\n        assert g(d + 1) / (d + 1) < g(d) / d, d\n    for d in range(5, N + 1):                                            # the g' recurrence\n        assert d * g_prime(d) == (d - 3) * g_prime(d - 1) + g_prime(d - 2), d\n    for d in range(4, N + 1):                                            # the sandwich\n        assert g_prime(d - 1) >= g_prime(d) >= g_prime(d - 1) / 3, d\n    for d in range(3, N + 1):                                            # coupled invariant\n        assert g(d - 1) <= g(d) <= (1 + g(d - 1)) / 2, d\n    out.append(f\"W1–W5 hold to n = {N} in exact rationals: recurrence (W1), g non-decreasing (W2), \"\n               f\"g' non-increasing from 3 (W3), property 6 (W4), 0 ≤ g < 1 and 0 ≤ g' ≤ 1/6 (W5), \"\n               f\"closed form (Lemma 8.1); also property 5, the g' recurrence n g'(n) = (n−3) g'(n−1) + g'(n−2) \"\n               f\"for n ≥ 5, the sandwich g'(n−1) ≥ g'(n) ≥ g'(n−1)/3 (n ≥ 4) and the coupled invariant \"\n               f\"g(n−1) ≤ g(n) ≤ (1 + g(n−1))/2 (n ≥ 3).\")\n    out.append(\"g(3..9) = \" + \", \".join(str(g(d)) for d in range(3, 10)))\n    out.append(\"g'(3..9) = \" + \", \".join(str(g_prime(d)) for d in range(3, 10)))\n    out.append(f\"A(1..6) = {[alternating_factorial(k) for k in range(1, 7)]}\")\n    return out\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# driver\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\ndef geng(n: int) -> list[str]:\n    return subprocess.run([\"nauty-geng\", \"-q\", str(n)], capture_output=True, text=True,\n                          check=True).stdout.splitlines()\n\n\ndef main() -> None:\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n    ap.add_argument(\"--max-n\", type=int, default=9)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--min-n\", type=int, default=1)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--workers\", type=int, default=8)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--no-stop\", action=\"store_true\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--log\", default=f\"{HERE}/check.log\")\n    a = ap.parse_args()\n\n    log = open(a.log, \"w\")\n\n    def say(s: str = \"\"):\n        print(s, flush=True)\n        log.write(s + \"\\n\")\n        log.flush()\n\n    say(f\"# item 02 brute-force check, {time.strftime('%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S UTC', time.gmtime())}, \"\n        f\"n = {a.min_n}..{a.max_n}, {a.workers} workers\")\n    for s in check_weights():\n        say(s)\n\n    violations: list[str] = []\n    per_n: dict[int, dict] = {}\n    t0 = time.time()\n    stop = False\n    with Pool(a.workers) as pool:\n        for n in range(a.min_n, a.max_n + 1):\n            lines = geng(n)\n            tn = time.time()\n            cnt: collections.Counter = collections.Counter()\n            mx: dict = {}\n            for res in pool.imap_unordered(one, list(enumerate(lines)), chunksize=64):\n                cnt.update(res[\"cnt\"])\n                for k, v in res[\"mx\"].items():\n                    if k not in mx or v > mx[k]:\n                        mx[k] = v\n                if res[\"viol\"]:\n                    hard = [v for v in res[\"viol\"] if not v.startswith(\"S1p-MEASURED\")]\n                    violations += res[\"viol\"]\n                    for v in res[\"viol\"]:\n                        say(\"VIOLATION \" + v if not v.startswith(\"S1p\") else \"MEASURED \" + v)\n                    if hard and not a.no_stop:\n                        stop = True\n                        break\n            per_n[n] = {\"cnt\": dict(cnt), \"mx\": {k: str(v) for k, v in mx.items()},\n                        \"seconds\": round(time.time() - tn, 1)}\n            say(f\"n={n}: {len(lines)} graphs in {time.time() - tn:.1f}s; \"\n                + \"; \".join(f\"{k}={v}\" for k, v in sorted(cnt.items()))\n                + \"; maxima \" + \", \".join(f\"{k}={v}\" for k, v in sorted(mx.items())))\n            if stop:\n                say(\"STOPPED on a violation\")\n                pool.terminate()\n                break\n    say(f\"total {time.time() - t0:.1f}s; violations (hard): \"\n        f\"{sum(1 for v in violations if not v.startswith('S1p'))}; \"\n        f\"S1′ measured failures: {sum(1 for v in violations if v.startswith('S1p'))}\")\n    with open(f\"{HERE}/violations.txt\", \"w\") as fh:\n        fh.write(\"# statement\\tgraph6\\tdetail  (S1p-MEASURED lines are the S1′ measurement, not violations)\\n\")\n        for v in violations:\n            fh.write(v + \"\\n\")\n    with open(f\"{HERE}/summary.json\", \"w\") as fh:\n        json.dump(per_n, fh, indent=1)\n    log.close()\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":21257,"cache_read_input_tokens":121732,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":21257,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8b20c5ed-4e93-4acb-9f13-261a84c24494","uuid":"28c56f95-fed8-4d73-958b-f58ba3e5e47e","timestamp":"2026-11-02T01:04:55.603Z","request_id":"req_011CgdCaNXEU9NxN9z4wGpK2","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01L8xuhMRHfyzAyYKbzRa1r3":{"file_path":"/home/al/dev/MOSP/reports/scratch/edwards_mcdermid/02_lemmas/check.py","content":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Brute-force check of every intermediate statement of the Edwards–McDermid\nchain (loop0012 item 02; `reports/edwards_mcdermid.md` §2; the plan is\n`reports/edwards_mcdermid_plan.md` §0.3–0.5) on every graph on 1–9 vertices\nfrom `nauty-geng`, pathwidth by the vertex-separation subset DP.\n\nThe statements, numbered as in the report's §2 (W = weights, C = cut lemma,\nP = potential, R = reduction system, S = step inequality, T = Theorem 3.2,\nA = assembly budgets, B = basic graphs, H = the shape of hypothesis (H3)):\n\n  W1–W5  recurrence, g non-decreasing, g' non-increasing from 3, property 6,\n         0 ≤ g < 1 and 0 ≤ g' ≤ 1/6, the closed form (exact rationals, to n = 40;\n         main process)\n  C1     pw(G) ≤ max(pw(G[V1]) + |∂1|, pw(G[V2]) + |∂2|, |∂1| + |∂2| − 1)\n         (every partition to 7 vertices; sampled partitions at 8–9); C1s is the\n         same without the middle term, measured only\n  C2     iterated form on a depth-2 bisection: pw(G) ≤ 2 Σ_i b_i + max_leaf pw\n  P1     f(G − w) = f(G) − g(d(w)) − Σ_{v ∈ N(w)} g'(d(v))        (every w)\n  P2     degrees 0 or ≥ 3, w of maximum degree Δ ≥ 4 with a neighbour of degree\n         ≤ Δ − 1 ⇒ f(G − w) ≤ f(G) − 1; Δ-regular, Δ ≥ 4 ⇒\n         f(G − w) = f(G) − 1 + g'(Δ − 1) − g'(Δ)\n  R1     every SPStep (at a vertex of degree 1 or 2) removes ≥ 1 edge\n  R2     every SPStep lowers no degree-count: deg_{H'}(u) ≤ deg_H(u) for all u,\n         hence f(H') ≤ f(H); a vertex of degree d isolated by the step loses g(d)\n  R3     commutation: SPStep H H' at v, w ≠ v ⇒ H' − w = H − w, or\n         H' − w = SPStep (H − w) at v (with v of degree 1 or 2 in H − w)\n  R5     a step at v inside a component acts on that component only\n  R6     one step costs at most one: pw(H) ≤ pw(H') + 1 (sampled at 9)\n  RU     (measured) every maximal reduction order reaches the same reduct\n  S0     the hinge: G* a reduced reduct of G' = G − w, v with d_{G'}(v) = d ≥ 3\n         ⇒ f(G') − f(G*) + g'(δ(G*)) ≥ g'(d)\n  S1     the step inequality for the paper's choice of w; S1′ for every\n         maximum-degree w (measured); both in the global-minimum form\n         1 + f(G*) − g'(δ(G*)) ≤ f(G) − g'(δ(G)), which implies the\n         per-component form 1 + f⁻(G*) ≤ f⁻(G)\n  SJ     the j-identity (paper (2)–(4)): 1 + f(G') = f(G) − j1 − j2 − j3\n  T1     Algorithm X: X, B with B non-empty, reduced, basic,\n         |X| + f⁻(B) ≤ f⁻(G); and (measured) r(G − X) = B\n  A1/A2  the budgets the record needs at n ≤ 9: max of pw − f⁻ over reduced\n         graphs and of pw − main term over all graphs, per n\n  B1     connected, every degree ≥ 3, not cubic ⇒ f⁻ ≥ 5/6; connected cubic ⇒\n         f⁻ = N/6 − 1/6; f⁻(component) ≥ 0; additivity over components\n  H3     pw(G) − pw(r(G)) per n (its maximum is the shape of (H3) at these sizes)\n\nA violation prints the graph6 string and stops (unless --no-stop).\n\n    nice -n 19 python3 reports/scratch/edwards_mcdermid/02_lemmas/check.py --max-n 9 --workers 8\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport collections\nimport json\nimport random\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nimport time\nfrom fractions import Fraction\nfrom multiprocessing import Pool\n\nsys.path.insert(0, \"/home/al/dev/MOSP\")\n\nfrom learning.edwards_mcdermid import (  # noqa: E402\n    alternating_factorial, bits, components, degrees, edge_count, f_potential,\n    fminus, g, g_closed_form, g_prime, is_cubic, is_reduced, min_degree, reduce,\n)\n\nHERE = \"/home/al/dev/MOSP/reports/scratch/edwards_mcdermid/02_lemmas\"\n\n# sampling at 8–9 vertices (the exhaustive partition sweep is 2^(n−1) DPs per\n# graph and does not fit the budget there; see the report)\nC1_PARTITIONS = 32      # random partitions per sampled graph at n = 8, 9\nC2_TREES = 4            # random depth-2 bisection trees per sampled graph\nSAMPLE_STRIDE_9 = 8     # at n = 9 the pathwidth-heavy checks run on every 8th graph\nRANDOM_ORDERS = {8: 200, 9: 60}   # reduction orders per graph for RU (200 below 8)\nS1_RANDOM_REDUCTS = 5   # random reducts of G − w for S1 beside the canonical one\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# graphs\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\ndef parse_g6(line: str) -> tuple[int, list[int]]:\n    b = line.strip().encode()\n    n = b[0] - 63\n    bitlist: list[int] = []\n    for ch in b[1:]:\n        v = ch - 63\n        bitlist += [(v >> i) & 1 for i in range(5, -1, -1)]\n    adj = [0] * n\n    k = 0\n    for j in range(1, n):\n        for i in range(j):\n            if bitlist[k]:\n                adj[i] |= 1 << j\n                adj[j] |= 1 << i\n            k += 1\n    return n, adj\n\n\ndef pw_induced(adj: list[int], S: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Vertex separation (= pathwidth) of G[S], by the subset DP over the\n    submasks of S in increasing numeric order.\"\"\"\n    if S == 0:\n        return 0\n    f = {0: 0}\n    T = (0 - S) & S\n    while True:\n        rest = S & ~T\n        cost = 0\n        U = T\n        while U:\n            low = U & -U\n            U ^= low\n            if adj[low.bit_length() - 1] & rest:\n                cost += 1\n        best = None\n        U = T\n        while U:\n            low = U & -U\n            U ^= low\n            c = f[T ^ low]\n            if best is None or c < best:\n                best = c\n        f[T] = cost if cost > best else best\n        if T == S:\n            break\n        T = (T - S) & S\n    return f[S]\n\n\ndef support(adj: list[int]) -> int:\n    m = 0\n    for v, a in enumerate(adj):\n        if a:\n            m |= 1 << v\n    return m\n\n\ndef isolate(adj: list[int], w: int) -> list[int]:\n    out = list(adj)\n    for u in bits(adj[w]):\n        out[u] &= ~(1 << w)\n    out[w] = 0\n    return out\n\n\ndef isolate_set(adj: list[int], X: int) -> list[int]:\n    out = list(adj)\n    for w in bits(X):\n        out = isolate(out, w)\n    return out\n\n\ndef sp_step(adj: list[int], v: int) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"One series-parallel operation at `v`, which must have degree 1 or 2.\"\"\"\n    d = adj[v].bit_count()\n    assert d in (1, 2), d\n    nb = adj[v]\n    out = isolate(adj, v)\n    if d == 2:\n        low = nb & -nb\n        x = low.bit_length() - 1\n        y = (nb ^ low).bit_length() - 1\n        if not (adj[x] >> y) & 1:\n            out[x] |= 1 << y\n            out[y] |= 1 << x\n    return out\n\n\ndef step_vertices(adj: list[int]) -> list[int]:\n    return [v for v in range(len(adj)) if 1 <= adj[v].bit_count() <= 2]\n\n\ndef reduce_random(adj: list[int], rng: random.Random) -> list[int]:\n    adj = list(adj)\n    while True:\n        cands = step_vertices(adj)\n        if not cands:\n            return adj\n        adj = sp_step(adj, rng.choice(cands))\n\n\ndef connected_on_support(adj: list[int]) -> bool:\n    return len(components(adj)) == 1\n\n\ndef is_empty(adj: list[int]) -> bool:\n    return not any(adj)\n\n\ndef global_min_degree(adj: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"δ over the support; 0 for the empty graph.\"\"\"\n    s = support(adj)\n    return min_degree(adj, s) if s else 0\n\n\ndef F_global(adj: list[int]) -> Fraction:\n    \"\"\"f(H) − g'(δ(H)) with δ over the support (the paper's one-component f⁻).\"\"\"\n    return f_potential(adj) - g_prime(global_min_degree(adj))\n\n\ndef restrict(adj: list[int], C: int) -> list[int]:\n    return [adj[v] & C if (C >> v) & 1 else 0 for v in range(len(adj))]\n\n\ndef is_basic_component(adj: list[int], C: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"`adj` restricted to its component `C` (every degree ≥ 3 there): cubic,\n    or some v ∈ C with r(G|C − v) empty.\"\"\"\n    sub = restrict(adj, C)\n    if is_cubic(sub, C):\n        return True\n    for v in bits(C):\n        radj, _ = reduce(isolate(sub, v))\n        if is_empty(radj):\n            return True\n    return False\n\n\ndef is_basic(adj: list[int]) -> bool:\n    return all(is_basic_component(adj, C) for C in components(adj))\n\n\ndef paper_choice(adj: list[int], C: int | None = None) -> tuple[list[int], list[int], int]:\n    \"\"\"Maximum-degree vertices (within `C` if given), those among them whose\n    lowest-degree neighbour has the smallest degree (the paper's rule), and Δ.\"\"\"\n    verts = list(bits(C)) if C is not None else [v for v in range(len(adj)) if adj[v]]\n    deg = degrees(adj)\n    Delta = max(deg[v] for v in verts)\n    maxs = [v for v in verts if deg[v] == Delta]\n    key = {v: min(deg[u] for u in bits(adj[v])) for v in maxs}\n    best = min(key.values())\n    return maxs, [v for v in maxs if key[v] == best], Delta\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# the per-graph worker\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\ndef one(args: tuple[int, str]) -> dict:\n    idx, line = args\n    n, adj = parse_g6(line)\n    rng = random.Random(idx * 1_000_003 + n)\n    cnt: collections.Counter = collections.Counter()\n    mx: dict[str, Fraction | int] = {}\n    viol: list[str] = []\n\n    def bump(key: str, value):\n        if key not in mx or value > mx[key]:\n            mx[key] = value\n\n    def bad(stmt: str, detail: str):\n        viol.append(f\"{stmt}\\t{line.strip()}\\t{detail}\")\n\n    deg = degrees(adj)\n    full = (1 << n) - 1\n    supp = support(adj)\n    heavy = n < 9 or idx % SAMPLE_STRIDE_9 == 0\n\n    # pathwidth of G and of r(G)\n    pw = pw_induced(adj, full)\n    radj, removed = reduce(adj)\n    pw_r = pw_induced(radj, support(radj))\n    cnt[\"graphs\"] += 1\n    gap = pw - pw_r\n    if gap < 0:\n        bad(\"H3-minor\", f\"pw={pw} pw_r={pw_r}\")\n    bump(\"H3_gap\", gap)\n    cnt[f\"H3_gap_{gap}\"] += 1\n    main_term = f_potential(radj)\n    bump(\"A2_pw_minus_main\", pw - main_term)\n    reduced = is_reduced(adj)\n    if reduced:\n        cnt[\"reduced\"] += 1\n        bump(\"A1_pw_minus_fminus\", pw - fminus(adj))\n        if gap != 0:\n            bad(\"H3-reduced\", \"a reduced graph is its own reduct\")\n\n    # ---- P1, P2: one deletion -------------------------------------------\n    f_G = f_potential(adj)\n    Delta = max(deg) if n else 0\n    for w in range(n):\n        Gw = isolate(adj, w)\n        lhs = f_potential(Gw)\n        rhs = f_G - g(deg[w]) - sum((g_prime(deg[v]) for v in bits(adj[w])), Fraction(0))\n        cnt[\"P1\"] += 1\n        if lhs != rhs:\n            bad(\"P1\", f\"w={w} lhs={lhs} rhs={rhs}\")\n        if reduced and deg[w] == Delta and Delta >= 4:\n            if any(deg[v] <= Delta - 1 for v in bits(adj[w])):\n                cnt[\"P2\"] += 1\n                if not lhs <= f_G - 1:\n                    bad(\"P2\", f\"w={w} f(G-w)={lhs} f(G)={f_G}\")\n            if all(deg[v] == Delta for v in range(n) if adj[v]):\n                cnt[\"P2reg\"] += 1\n                if lhs != f_G - 1 + g_prime(Delta - 1) - g_prime(Delta):\n                    bad(\"P2reg\", f\"w={w} f(G-w)={lhs} f(G)={f_G} Delta={Delta}\")\n\n    # ---- R1, R2, R3, R5, R6: one step ----------------------------------\n    steps = step_vertices(adj)\n    comps = components(adj)\n    comp_of = {}\n    for C in comps:\n        for v in bits(C):\n            comp_of[v] = C\n    m_G = edge_count(adj)\n    for v in steps:\n        H2 = sp_step(adj, v)\n        cnt[\"R1\"] += 1\n        if not edge_count(H2) <= m_G - 1:\n            bad(\"R1\", f\"v={v}\")\n        d2 = degrees(H2)\n        cnt[\"R2\"] += 1\n        if any(d2[u] > deg[u] for u in range(n)):\n            bad(\"R2\", f\"v={v} degree rose\")\n        if not f_potential(H2) <= f_G:\n            bad(\"R2f\", f\"v={v}\")\n        if not f_G - f_potential(H2) >= g(deg[v]):\n            bad(\"R2iso\", f\"v={v}\")\n        # R3\n        for w in range(n):\n            if w == v:\n                continue\n            cnt[\"R3\"] += 1\n            Hw = isolate(adj, w)\n            H2w = isolate(H2, w)\n            if H2w == Hw:\n                cnt[\"R3_zero\"] += 1\n            elif 1 <= Hw[v].bit_count() <= 2 and sp_step(Hw, v) == H2w:\n                cnt[\"R3_one\"] += 1\n            else:\n                bad(\"R3\", f\"v={v} w={w}\")\n        # R5\n        if len(comps) >= 2:\n            C = comp_of[v]\n            cnt[\"R5\"] += 1\n            inside = restrict(adj, C)\n            outside = [adj[u] & ~C for u in range(n)]\n            lifted = sp_step(inside, v)\n            if [lifted[u] | outside[u] for u in range(n)] != H2:\n                bad(\"R5\", f\"v={v}\")\n        # R6 (pathwidth-heavy, sampled at 9)\n        if heavy:\n            cnt[\"R6\"] += 1\n            pw2 = pw_induced(H2, support(H2))\n            if not pw <= pw2 + 1:\n                bad(\"R6\", f\"v={v} pw={pw} pw'={pw2}\")\n            bump(\"R6_drop\", pw - pw2)\n\n    # ---- RU: uniqueness of the reduct -----------------------------------\n    if steps:\n        k = RANDOM_ORDERS.get(n, 200)\n        same = True\n        for _ in range(k):\n            if reduce_random(adj, rng) != radj:\n                same = False\n                break\n        cnt[\"RU_graphs\"] += 1\n        cnt[\"RU_orders\"] += k\n        if not same:\n            cnt[\"RU_nonunique\"] += 1\n\n    # ---- B1, additivity -------------------------------------------------\n    fm = fminus(adj)\n    tot = Fraction(0)\n    for C in comps:\n        sub = restrict(adj, C)\n        fc = fminus(sub)\n        tot += fc\n        cnt[\"B1_nonneg\"] += 1\n        if fc < 0:\n            bad(\"B1neg\", f\"component {C:b} fminus={fc}\")\n    cnt[\"B1_add\"] += 1\n    if tot != fm:\n        bad(\"B1add\", f\"sum={tot} fminus={fm}\")\n    connected = len(comps) == 1\n    min3 = bool(supp) and all(d == 0 or d >= 3 for d in deg)\n    if connected and min3:\n        if is_cubic(adj, supp):\n            N = supp.bit_count()\n            cnt[\"B1_cubic\"] += 1\n            if fm != Fraction(N, 6) - Fraction(1, 6):\n                bad(\"B1cubic\", f\"fminus={fm} N={N}\")\n        else:\n            cnt[\"B1_noncubic\"] += 1\n            if fm < Fraction(5, 6):\n                bad(\"B1floor\", f\"fminus={fm}\")\n\n    # ---- S0, S1, S1′, SJ: the step ----------------------------------------\n    if connected and min3:\n        basic = is_basic(adj)\n        cnt[\"S_conn_min3\"] += 1\n        if basic:\n            cnt[\"S_basic\"] += 1\n        else:\n            cnt[\"S_nonbasic\"] += 1\n            maxs, chosen, D = paper_choice(adj)\n            assert D >= 4\n            FG = F_global(adj)\n            for w in maxs:\n                Gp = isolate(adj, w)\n                dp = degrees(Gp)\n                reducts = [reduce(Gp)[0]]\n                for _ in range(S1_RANDOM_REDUCTS):\n                    r = reduce_random(Gp, rng)\n                    if r not in reducts:\n                        reducts.append(r)\n                nbrs = sorted(bits(adj[w]), key=lambda v: deg[v])\n                j1 = g_prime(deg[nbrs[0]]) - g_prime(D - 1)\n                j2 = g_prime(deg[nbrs[1]]) - g_prime(D)\n                j3 = sum((g_prime(deg[v]) - g_prime(D) for v in nbrs[2:]), Fraction(0))\n                cnt[\"SJ\"] += 1\n                if 1 + f_potential(Gp) != f_G - j1 - j2 - j3:\n                    bad(\"SJ\", f\"w={w}\")\n                for Gs in reducts:\n                    if is_empty(Gs):\n                        bad(\"S-empty\", f\"w={w}: G* empty though G is not basic\")\n                        continue\n                    f_Gs = f_potential(Gs)\n                    gd = g_prime(global_min_degree(Gs))\n                    # S0 for every v of degree ≥ 3 in G'\n                    for v in range(n):\n                        if dp[v] >= 3:\n                            cnt[\"S0\"] += 1\n                            if not f_potential(Gp) - f_Gs + gd >= g_prime(dp[v]):\n                                bad(\"S0\", f\"w={w} v={v}\")\n                    ok = 1 + f_Gs - gd <= FG\n                    okc = 1 + fminus(Gs) <= fm\n                    if w in chosen:\n                        cnt[\"S1\"] += 1\n                        if not ok:\n                            bad(\"S1\", f\"w={w} 1+F(G*)={1 + f_Gs - gd} F(G)={FG}\")\n                        if not okc:\n                            bad(\"S1c\", f\"w={w}\")\n                    cnt[\"S1p\"] += 1\n                    if not ok:\n                        cnt[\"S1p_fail\"] += 1\n                        if cnt[\"S1p_fail\"] == 1:\n                            cnt[\"S1p_first\"] = 0\n                            viol.append(f\"S1p-MEASURED\\t{line.strip()}\\tw={w} 1+F(G*)={1 + f_Gs - gd} F(G)={FG}\")\n                    if not okc:\n                        cnt[\"S1pc_fail\"] += 1\n\n    # ---- T1: Algorithm X -------------------------------------------------\n    if reduced and supp:\n        cnt[\"T1\"] += 1\n        X = 0\n        cur = list(adj)\n        while True:\n            comps_cur = components(cur)\n            nonbasic = [C for C in comps_cur if not is_basic_component(cur, C)]\n            if not nonbasic:\n                break\n            C = nonbasic[0]\n            _, chosen, _ = paper_choice(cur, C)\n            w = rng.choice(chosen)\n            X |= 1 << w\n            cur, _ = reduce(isolate(cur, w))\n        B = cur\n        if is_empty(B):\n            bad(\"T1empty\", f\"X={X:b}\")\n        if not is_reduced(B):\n            bad(\"T1reduced\", f\"X={X:b}\")\n        if not is_basic(B):\n            bad(\"T1basic\", f\"X={X:b}\")\n        if not X.bit_count() + fminus(B) <= fm:\n            bad(\"T1\", f\"X={X:b} |X|+fminus(B)={X.bit_count() + fminus(B)} fminus(G)={fm}\")\n        if X & ~supp:\n            bad(\"T1supp\", f\"X={X:b}\")\n        direct, _ = reduce(isolate_set(adj, X))\n        cnt[\"T1_direct\"] += 1\n        if direct != B:\n            cnt[\"T1_direct_differs\"] += 1\n        bump(\"T1_X\", X.bit_count())\n\n    # ---- C1, C2: the cut lemma --------------------------------------------\n    if heavy:\n        if n <= 7:\n            parts = range(0, 1 << (n - 1))     # V1 ∌ vertex n−1: each partition once\n        else:\n            parts = [rng.randrange(0, 1 << (n - 1)) for _ in range(C1_PARTITIONS)]\n        pwcache: dict[int, int] = {full: pw, 0: 0}\n\n        def pwS(S: int) -> int:\n            if S not in pwcache:\n                pwcache[S] = pw_induced(adj, S)\n            return pwcache[S]\n\n        for V1 in parts:\n            V2 = full & ~V1\n            b1 = sum(1 for v in bits(V1) if adj[v] & V2)\n            b2 = sum(1 for v in bits(V2) if adj[v] & V1)\n            bound = max(pwS(V1) + b1, pwS(V2) + b2, b1 + b2 - 1)\n            cnt[\"C1\"] += 1\n            if not pw <= bound:\n                bad(\"C1\", f\"V1={V1:b} pw={pw} bound={bound}\")\n            if pw <= max(pwS(V1) + b1, pwS(V2) + b2):\n                cnt[\"C1s_holds\"] += 1\n            bump(\"C1_slack\", bound - pw)\n        # C2: depth-2 bisection trees (random), budgets b_i = max boundary at level i\n        if n >= 4:\n            for _ in range(C2_TREES):\n                V1 = rng.randrange(0, 1 << (n - 1))\n                V2 = full & ~V1\n                lvl1 = max(sum(1 for v in bits(V1) if adj[v] & V2),\n                           sum(1 for v in bits(V2) if adj[v] & V1))\n                lvl2 = 0\n                leaves = []\n                for P in (V1, V2):\n                    pb = list(bits(P))\n                    sub = 0\n                    for v in pb:\n                        if rng.random() < 0.5:\n                            sub |= 1 << v\n                    Q1, Q2 = sub, P & ~sub\n                    lvl2 = max(lvl2,\n                               sum(1 for v in bits(Q1) if adj[v] & Q2),\n                               sum(1 for v in bits(Q2) if adj[v] & Q1))\n                    leaves += [pwS(Q1), pwS(Q2)]\n                bound = 2 * (lvl1 + lvl2) + max(leaves)\n                cnt[\"C2\"] += 1\n                if not pw <= bound:\n                    bad(\"C2\", f\"pw={pw} bound={bound}\")\n\n    return {\"n\": n, \"cnt\": cnt, \"mx\": mx, \"viol\": viol}\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# W1–W5 (main process)\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\ndef check_weights(N: int = 40) -> list[str]:\n    out = []\n    for d in range(4, N + 1):\n        assert d * g(d) == (d - 2) * g(d - 1) + g(d - 2) + 1, d          # W1\n    for d in range(0, N):\n        assert g(d + 1) >= g(d), d                                       # W2 (Lemma 8.3)\n    for d in range(3, N):\n        assert g_prime(d + 1) <= g_prime(d), d                           # W3 (Lemma 8.4)\n    for d in range(4, N + 1):\n        assert 1 - g(d) == (d - 1) * g_prime(d) + g_prime(d - 1), d      # W4 (property 6)\n    for d in range(0, N + 1):\n        assert 0 <= g(d) < 1, d                                          # W5a\n        assert 0 <= g_prime(d) <= Fraction(1, 6), d                      # W5b\n    for d in range(2, N + 1):\n        assert g_closed_form(d) == g(d), d                               # W5c (Lemma 8.1)\n    for d in range(5, N):                                                # property 5 (not used)\n        assert g(d + 1) / (d + 1) < g(d) / d, d\n    for d in range(5, N + 1):                                            # the g' recurrence\n        assert d * g_prime(d) == (d - 3) * g_prime(d - 1) + g_prime(d - 2), d\n    for d in range(4, N + 1):                                            # the sandwich\n        assert g_prime(d - 1) >= g_prime(d) >= g_prime(d - 1) / 3, d\n    for d in range(3, N + 1):                                            # coupled invariant\n        assert g(d - 1) <= g(d) <= (1 + g(d - 1)) / 2, d\n    out.append(f\"W1–W5 hold to n = {N} in exact rationals: recurrence (W1), g non-decreasing (W2), \"\n               f\"g' non-increasing from 3 (W3), property 6 (W4), 0 ≤ g < 1 and 0 ≤ g' ≤ 1/6 (W5), \"\n               f\"closed form (Lemma 8.1); also property 5, the g' recurrence n g'(n) = (n−3) g'(n−1) + g'(n−2) \"\n               f\"for n ≥ 5, the sandwich g'(n−1) ≥ g'(n) ≥ g'(n−1)/3 (n ≥ 4) and the coupled invariant \"\n               f\"g(n−1) ≤ g(n) ≤ (1 + g(n−1))/2 (n ≥ 3).\")\n    out.append(\"g(3..9) = \" + \", \".join(str(g(d)) for d in range(3, 10)))\n    out.append(\"g'(3..9) = \" + \", \".join(str(g_prime(d)) for d in range(3, 10)))\n    out.append(f\"A(1..6) = {[alternating_factorial(k) for k in range(1, 7)]}\")\n    return out\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# driver\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\ndef geng(n: int) -> list[str]:\n    return subprocess.run([\"nauty-geng\", \"-q\", str(n)], capture_output=True, text=True,\n                          check=True).stdout.splitlines()\n\n\ndef main() -> None:\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n    ap.add_argument(\"--max-n\", type=int, default=9)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--min-n\", type=int, default=1)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--workers\", type=int, default=8)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--no-stop\", action=\"store_true\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--log\", default=f\"{HERE}/check.log\")\n    a = ap.parse_args()\n\n    log = open(a.log, \"w\")\n\n    def say(s: str = \"\"):\n        print(s, flush=True)\n        log.write(s + \"\\n\")\n        log.flush()\n\n    say(f\"# item 02 brute-force check, {time.strftime('%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S UTC', time.gmtime())}, \"\n        f\"n = {a.min_n}..{a.max_n}, {a.workers} workers\")\n    for s in check_weights():\n        say(s)\n\n    violations: list[str] = []\n    per_n: dict[int, dict] = {}\n    t0 = time.time()\n    stop = False\n    with Pool(a.workers) as pool:\n        for n in range(a.min_n, a.max_n + 1):\n            lines = geng(n)\n            tn = time.time()\n            cnt: collections.Counter = collections.Counter()\n            mx: dict = {}\n            for res in pool.imap_unordered(one, list(enumerate(lines)), chunksize=64):\n                cnt.update(res[\"cnt\"])\n                for k, v in res[\"mx\"].items():\n                    if k not in mx or v > mx[k]:\n                        mx[k] = v\n                if res[\"viol\"]:\n                    hard = [v for v in res[\"viol\"] if not v.startswith(\"S1p-MEASURED\")]\n                    violations += res[\"viol\"]\n                    for v in res[\"viol\"]:\n                        say(\"VIOLATION \" + v if not v.startswith(\"S1p\") else \"MEASURED \" + v)\n                    if hard and not a.no_stop:\n                        stop = True\n                        break\n            per_n[n] = {\"cnt\": dict(cnt), \"mx\": {k: str(v) for k, v in mx.items()},\n                        \"seconds\": round(time.time() - tn, 1)}\n            say(f\"n={n}: {len(lines)} graphs in {time.time() - tn:.1f}s; \"\n                + \"; \".join(f\"{k}={v}\" for k, v in sorted(cnt.items()))\n                + \"; maxima \" + \", \".join(f\"{k}={v}\" for k, v in sorted(mx.items())))\n            if stop:\n                say(\"STOPPED on a violation\")\n                pool.terminate()\n                break\n    say(f\"total {time.time() - t0:.1f}s; violations (hard): \"\n        f\"{sum(1 for v in violations if not v.startswith('S1p'))}; \"\n        f\"S1′ measured failures: {sum(1 for v in violations if v.startswith('S1p'))}\")\n    with open(f\"{HERE}/violations.txt\", \"w\") as fh:\n        fh.write(\"# statement\\tgraph6\\tdetail  (S1p-MEASURED lines are the S1′ measurement, not violations)\\n\")\n        for v in violations:\n            fh.write(v + \"\\n\")\n    with open(f\"{HERE}/summary.json\", \"w\") as fh:\n        json.dump(per_n, fh, indent=1)\n    log.close()\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01L8xuhMRHfyzAyYKbzRa1r3","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /home/al/dev/MOSP/reports/scratch/edwards_mcdermid/02_lemmas/check.py (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8b20c5ed-4e93-4acb-9f13-261a84c24494","uuid":"d7575f62-3f39-4361-8a50-260a157a4582","timestamp":"2026-11-02T01:04:55.627Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"create","filePath":"/home/al/dev/MOSP/reports/scratch/edwards_mcdermid/02_lemmas/check.py","content":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Brute-force check of every intermediate statement of the Edwards–McDermid\nchain (loop0012 item 02; `reports/edwards_mcdermid.md` §2; the plan is\n`reports/edwards_mcdermid_plan.md` §0.3–0.5) on every graph on 1–9 vertices\nfrom `nauty-geng`, pathwidth by the vertex-separation subset DP.\n\nThe statements, numbered as in the report's §2 (W = weights, C = cut lemma,\nP = potential, R = reduction system, S = step inequality, T = Theorem 3.2,\nA = assembly budgets, B = basic graphs, H = the shape of hypothesis (H3)):\n\n  W1–W5  recurrence, g non-decreasing, g' non-increasing from 3, property 6,\n         0 ≤ g < 1 and 0 ≤ g' ≤ 1/6, the closed form (exact rationals, to n = 40;\n         main process)\n  C1     pw(G) ≤ max(pw(G[V1]) + |∂1|, pw(G[V2]) + |∂2|, |∂1| + |∂2| − 1)\n         (every partition to 7 vertices; sampled partitions at 8–9); C1s is the\n         same without the middle term, measured only\n  C2     iterated form on a depth-2 bisection: pw(G) ≤ 2 Σ_i b_i + max_leaf pw\n  P1     f(G − w) = f(G) − g(d(w)) − Σ_{v ∈ N(w)} g'(d(v))        (every w)\n  P2     degrees 0 or ≥ 3, w of maximum degree Δ ≥ 4 with a neighbour of degree\n         ≤ Δ − 1 ⇒ f(G − w) ≤ f(G) − 1; Δ-regular, Δ ≥ 4 ⇒\n         f(G − w) = f(G) − 1 + g'(Δ − 1) − g'(Δ)\n  R1     every SPStep (at a vertex of degree 1 or 2) removes ≥ 1 edge\n  R2     every SPStep lowers no degree-count: deg_{H'}(u) ≤ deg_H(u) for all u,\n         hence f(H') ≤ f(H); a vertex of degree d isolated by the step loses g(d)\n  R3     commutation: SPStep H H' at v, w ≠ v ⇒ H' − w = H − w, or\n         H' − w = SPStep (H − w) at v (with v of degree 1 or 2 in H − w)\n  R5     a step at v inside a component acts on that component only\n  R6     one step costs at most one: pw(H) ≤ pw(H') + 1 (sampled at 9)\n  RU     (measured) every maximal reduction order reaches the same reduct\n  S0     the hinge: G* a reduced reduct of G' = G − w, v with d_{G'}(v) = d ≥ 3\n         ⇒ f(G') − f(G*) + g'(δ(G*)) ≥ g'(d)\n  S1     the step inequality for the paper's choice of w; S1′ for every\n         maximum-degree w (measured); both in the global-minimum form\n         1 + f(G*) − g'(δ(G*)) ≤ f(G) − g'(δ(G)), which implies the\n         per-component form 1 + f⁻(G*) ≤ f⁻(G)\n  SJ     the j-identity (paper (2)–(4)): 1 + f(G') = f(G) − j1 − j2 − j3\n  T1     Algorithm X: X, B with B non-empty, reduced, basic,\n         |X| + f⁻(B) ≤ f⁻(G); and (measured) r(G − X) = B\n  A1/A2  the budgets the record needs at n ≤ 9: max of pw − f⁻ over reduced\n         graphs and of pw − main term over all graphs, per n\n  B1     connected, every degree ≥ 3, not cubic ⇒ f⁻ ≥ 5/6; connected cubic ⇒\n         f⁻ = N/6 − 1/6; f⁻(component) ≥ 0; additivity over components\n  H3     pw(G) − pw(r(G)) per n (its maximum is the shape of (H3) at these sizes)\n\nA violation prints the graph6 string and stops (unless --no-stop).\n\n    nice -n 19 python3 reports/scratch/edwards_mcdermid/02_lemmas/check.py --max-n 9 --workers 8\n\"\"\"\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport collections\nimport json\nimport random\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nimport time\nfrom fractions import Fraction\nfrom multiprocessing import Pool\n\nsys.path.insert(0, \"/home/al/dev/MOSP\")\n\nfrom learning.edwards_mcdermid import (  # noqa: E402\n    alternating_factorial, bits, components, degrees, edge_count, f_potential,\n    fminus, g, g_closed_form, g_prime, is_cubic, is_reduced, min_degree, reduce,\n)\n\nHERE = \"/home/al/dev/MOSP/reports/scratch/edwards_mcdermid/02_lemmas\"\n\n# sampling at 8–9 vertices (the exhaustive partition sweep is 2^(n−1) DPs per\n# graph and does not fit the budget there; see the report)\nC1_PARTITIONS = 32      # random partitions per sampled graph at n = 8, 9\nC2_TREES = 4            # random depth-2 bisection trees per sampled graph\nSAMPLE_STRIDE_9 = 8     # at n = 9 the pathwidth-heavy checks run on every 8th graph\nRANDOM_ORDERS = {8: 200, 9: 60}   # reduction orders per graph for RU (200 below 8)\nS1_RANDOM_REDUCTS = 5   # random reducts of G − w for S1 beside the canonical one\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# graphs\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\ndef parse_g6(line: str) -> tuple[int, list[int]]:\n    b = line.strip().encode()\n    n = b[0] - 63\n    bitlist: list[int] = []\n    for ch in b[1:]:\n        v = ch - 63\n        bitlist += [(v >> i) & 1 for i in range(5, -1, -1)]\n    adj = [0] * n\n    k = 0\n    for j in range(1, n):\n        for i in range(j):\n            if bitlist[k]:\n                adj[i] |= 1 << j\n                adj[j] |= 1 << i\n            k += 1\n    return n, adj\n\n\ndef pw_induced(adj: list[int], S: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Vertex separation (= pathwidth) of G[S], by the subset DP over the\n    submasks of S in increasing numeric order.\"\"\"\n    if S == 0:\n        return 0\n    f = {0: 0}\n    T = (0 - S) & S\n    while True:\n        rest = S & ~T\n        cost = 0\n        U = T\n        while U:\n            low = U & -U\n            U ^= low\n            if adj[low.bit_length() - 1] & rest:\n                cost += 1\n        best = None\n        U = T\n        while U:\n            low = U & -U\n            U ^= low\n            c = f[T ^ low]\n            if best is None or c < best:\n                best = c\n        f[T] = cost if cost > best else best\n        if T == S:\n            break\n        T = (T - S) & S\n    return f[S]\n\n\ndef support(adj: list[int]) -> int:\n    m = 0\n    for v, a in enumerate(adj):\n        if a:\n            m |= 1 << v\n    return m\n\n\ndef isolate(adj: list[int], w: int) -> list[int]:\n    out = list(adj)\n    for u in bits(adj[w]):\n        out[u] &= ~(1 << w)\n    out[w] = 0\n    return out\n\n\ndef isolate_set(adj: list[int], X: int) -> list[int]:\n    out = list(adj)\n    for w in bits(X):\n        out = isolate(out, w)\n    return out\n\n\ndef sp_step(adj: list[int], v: int) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"One series-parallel operation at `v`, which must have degree 1 or 2.\"\"\"\n    d = adj[v].bit_count()\n    assert d in (1, 2), d\n    nb = adj[v]\n    out = isolate(adj, v)\n    if d == 2:\n        low = nb & -nb\n        x = low.bit_length() - 1\n        y = (nb ^ low).bit_length() - 1\n        if not (adj[x] >> y) & 1:\n            out[x] |= 1 << y\n            out[y] |= 1 << x\n    return out\n\n\ndef step_vertices(adj: list[int]) -> list[int]:\n    return [v for v in range(len(adj)) if 1 <= adj[v].bit_count() <= 2]\n\n\ndef reduce_random(adj: list[int], rng: random.Random) -> list[int]:\n    adj = list(adj)\n    while True:\n        cands = step_vertices(adj)\n        if not cands:\n            return adj\n        adj = sp_step(adj, rng.choice(cands))\n\n\ndef connected_on_support(adj: list[int]) -> bool:\n    return len(components(adj)) == 1\n\n\ndef is_empty(adj: list[int]) -> bool:\n    return not any(adj)\n\n\ndef global_min_degree(adj: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"δ over the support; 0 for the empty graph.\"\"\"\n    s = support(adj)\n    return min_degree(adj, s) if s else 0\n\n\ndef F_global(adj: list[int]) -> Fraction:\n    \"\"\"f(H) − g'(δ(H)) with δ over the support (the paper's one-component f⁻).\"\"\"\n    return f_potential(adj) - g_prime(global_min_degree(adj))\n\n\ndef restrict(adj: list[int], C: int) -> list[int]:\n    return [adj[v] & C if (C >> v) & 1 else 0 for v in range(len(adj))]\n\n\ndef is_basic_component(adj: list[int], C: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"`adj` restricted to its component `C` (every degree ≥ 3 there): cubic,\n    or some v ∈ C with r(G|C − v) empty.\"\"\"\n    sub = restrict(adj, C)\n    if is_cubic(sub, C):\n        return True\n    for v in bits(C):\n        radj, _ = reduce(isolate(sub, v))\n        if is_empty(radj):\n            return True\n    return False\n\n\ndef is_basic(adj: list[int]) -> bool:\n    return all(is_basic_component(adj, C) for C in components(adj))\n\n\ndef paper_choice(adj: list[int], C: int | None = None) -> tuple[list[int], list[int], int]:\n    \"\"\"Maximum-degree vertices (within `C` if given), those among them whose\n    lowest-degree neighbour has the smallest degree (the paper's rule), and Δ.\"\"\"\n    verts = list(bits(C)) if C is not None else [v for v in range(len(adj)) if adj[v]]\n    deg = degrees(adj)\n    Delta = max(deg[v] for v in verts)\n    maxs = [v for v in verts if deg[v] == Delta]\n    key = {v: min(deg[u] for u in bits(adj[v])) for v in maxs}\n    best = min(key.values())\n    return maxs, [v for v in maxs if key[v] == best], Delta\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# the per-graph worker\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\ndef one(args: tuple[int, str]) -> dict:\n    idx, line = args\n    n, adj = parse_g6(line)\n    rng = random.Random(idx * 1_000_003 + n)\n    cnt: collections.Counter = collections.Counter()\n    mx: dict[str, Fraction | int] = {}\n    viol: list[str] = []\n\n    def bump(key: str, value):\n        if key not in mx or value > mx[key]:\n            mx[key] = value\n\n    def bad(stmt: str, detail: str):\n        viol.append(f\"{stmt}\\t{line.strip()}\\t{detail}\")\n\n    deg = degrees(adj)\n    full = (1 << n) - 1\n    supp = support(adj)\n    heavy = n < 9 or idx % SAMPLE_STRIDE_9 == 0\n\n    # pathwidth of G and of r(G)\n    pw = pw_induced(adj, full)\n    radj, removed = reduce(adj)\n    pw_r = pw_induced(radj, support(radj))\n    cnt[\"graphs\"] += 1\n    gap = pw - pw_r\n    if gap < 0:\n        bad(\"H3-minor\", f\"pw={pw} pw_r={pw_r}\")\n    bump(\"H3_gap\", gap)\n    cnt[f\"H3_gap_{gap}\"] += 1\n    main_term = f_potential(radj)\n    bump(\"A2_pw_minus_main\", pw - main_term)\n    reduced = is_reduced(adj)\n    if reduced:\n        cnt[\"reduced\"] += 1\n        bump(\"A1_pw_minus_fminus\", pw - fminus(adj))\n        if gap != 0:\n            bad(\"H3-reduced\", \"a reduced graph is its own reduct\")\n\n    # ---- P1, P2: one deletion -------------------------------------------\n    f_G = f_potential(adj)\n    Delta = max(deg) if n else 0\n    for w in range(n):\n        Gw = isolate(adj, w)\n        lhs = f_potential(Gw)\n        rhs = f_G - g(deg[w]) - sum((g_prime(deg[v]) for v in bits(adj[w])), Fraction(0))\n        cnt[\"P1\"] += 1\n        if lhs != rhs:\n            bad(\"P1\", f\"w={w} lhs={lhs} rhs={rhs}\")\n        if reduced and deg[w] == Delta and Delta >= 4:\n            if any(deg[v] <= Delta - 1 for v in bits(adj[w])):\n                cnt[\"P2\"] += 1\n                if not lhs <= f_G - 1:\n                    bad(\"P2\", f\"w={w} f(G-w)={lhs} f(G)={f_G}\")\n            if all(deg[v] == Delta for v in range(n) if adj[v]):\n                cnt[\"P2reg\"] += 1\n                if lhs != f_G - 1 + g_prime(Delta - 1) - g_prime(Delta):\n                    bad(\"P2reg\", f\"w={w} f(G-w)={lhs} f(G)={f_G} Delta={Delta}\")\n\n    # ---- R1, R2, R3, R5, R6: one step ----------------------------------\n    steps = step_vertices(adj)\n    comps = components(adj)\n    comp_of = {}\n    for C in comps:\n        for v in bits(C):\n            comp_of[v] = C\n    m_G = edge_count(adj)\n    for v in steps:\n        H2 = sp_step(adj, v)\n        cnt[\"R1\"] += 1\n        if not edge_count(H2) <= m_G - 1:\n            bad(\"R1\", f\"v={v}\")\n        d2 = degrees(H2)\n        cnt[\"R2\"] += 1\n        if any(d2[u] > deg[u] for u in range(n)):\n            bad(\"R2\", f\"v={v} degree rose\")\n        if not f_potential(H2) <= f_G:\n            bad(\"R2f\", f\"v={v}\")\n        if not f_G - f_potential(H2) >= g(deg[v]):\n            bad(\"R2iso\", f\"v={v}\")\n        # R3\n        for w in range(n):\n            if w == v:\n                continue\n            cnt[\"R3\"] += 1\n            Hw = isolate(adj, w)\n            H2w = isolate(H2, w)\n            if H2w == Hw:\n                cnt[\"R3_zero\"] += 1\n            elif 1 <= Hw[v].bit_count() <= 2 and sp_step(Hw, v) == H2w:\n                cnt[\"R3_one\"] += 1\n            else:\n                bad(\"R3\", f\"v={v} w={w}\")\n        # R5\n        if len(comps) >= 2:\n            C = comp_of[v]\n            cnt[\"R5\"] += 1\n            inside = restrict(adj, C)\n            outside = [adj[u] & ~C for u in range(n)]\n            lifted = sp_step(inside, v)\n            if [lifted[u] | outside[u] for u in range(n)] != H2:\n                bad(\"R5\", f\"v={v}\")\n        # R6 (pathwidth-heavy, sampled at 9)\n        if heavy:\n            cnt[\"R6\"] += 1\n            pw2 = pw_induced(H2, support(H2))\n            if not pw <= pw2 + 1:\n                bad(\"R6\", f\"v={v} pw={pw} pw'={pw2}\")\n            bump(\"R6_drop\", pw - pw2)\n\n    # ---- RU: uniqueness of the reduct -----------------------------------\n    if steps:\n        k = RANDOM_ORDERS.get(n, 200)\n        same = True\n        for _ in range(k):\n            if reduce_random(adj, rng) != radj:\n                same = False\n                break\n        cnt[\"RU_graphs\"] += 1\n        cnt[\"RU_orders\"] += k\n        if not same:\n            cnt[\"RU_nonunique\"] += 1\n\n    # ---- B1, additivity -------------------------------------------------\n    fm = fminus(adj)\n    tot = Fraction(0)\n    for C in comps:\n        sub = restrict(adj, C)\n        fc = fminus(sub)\n        tot += fc\n        cnt[\"B1_nonneg\"] += 1\n        if fc < 0:\n            bad(\"B1neg\", f\"component {C:b} fminus={fc}\")\n    cnt[\"B1_add\"] += 1\n    if tot != fm:\n        bad(\"B1add\", f\"sum={tot} fminus={fm}\")\n    connected = len(comps) == 1\n    min3 = bool(supp) and all(d == 0 or d >= 3 for d in deg)\n    if connected and min3:\n        if is_cubic(adj, supp):\n            N = supp.bit_count()\n            cnt[\"B1_cubic\"] += 1\n            if fm != Fraction(N, 6) - Fraction(1, 6):\n                bad(\"B1cubic\", f\"fminus={fm} N={N}\")\n        else:\n            cnt[\"B1_noncubic\"] += 1\n            if fm < Fraction(5, 6):\n                bad(\"B1floor\", f\"fminus={fm}\")\n\n    # ---- S0, S1, S1′, SJ: the step ----------------------------------------\n    if connected and min3:\n        basic = is_basic(adj)\n        cnt[\"S_conn_min3\"] += 1\n        if basic:\n            cnt[\"S_basic\"] += 1\n        else:\n            cnt[\"S_nonbasic\"] += 1\n            maxs, chosen, D = paper_choice(adj)\n            assert D >= 4\n            FG = F_global(adj)\n            for w in maxs:\n                Gp = isolate(adj, w)\n                dp = degrees(Gp)\n                reducts = [reduce(Gp)[0]]\n                for _ in range(S1_RANDOM_REDUCTS):\n                    r = reduce_random(Gp, rng)\n                    if r not in reducts:\n                        reducts.append(r)\n                nbrs = sorted(bits(adj[w]), key=lambda v: deg[v])\n                j1 = g_prime(deg[nbrs[0]]) - g_prime(D - 1)\n                j2 = g_prime(deg[nbrs[1]]) - g_prime(D)\n                j3 = sum((g_prime(deg[v]) - g_prime(D) for v in nbrs[2:]), Fraction(0))\n                cnt[\"SJ\"] += 1\n                if 1 + f_potential(Gp) != f_G - j1 - j2 - j3:\n                    bad(\"SJ\", f\"w={w}\")\n                for Gs in reducts:\n                    if is_empty(Gs):\n                        bad(\"S-empty\", f\"w={w}: G* empty though G is not basic\")\n                        continue\n                    f_Gs = f_potential(Gs)\n                    gd = g_prime(global_min_degree(Gs))\n                    # S0 for every v of degree ≥ 3 in G'\n                    for v in range(n):\n                        if dp[v] >= 3:\n                            cnt[\"S0\"] += 1\n                            if not f_potential(Gp) - f_Gs + gd >= g_prime(dp[v]):\n                                bad(\"S0\", f\"w={w} v={v}\")\n                    ok = 1 + f_Gs - gd <= FG\n                    okc = 1 + fminus(Gs) <= fm\n                    if w in chosen:\n                        cnt[\"S1\"] += 1\n                        if not ok:\n                            bad(\"S1\", f\"w={w} 1+F(G*)={1 + f_Gs - gd} F(G)={FG}\")\n                        if not okc:\n                            bad(\"S1c\", f\"w={w}\")\n                    cnt[\"S1p\"] += 1\n                    if not ok:\n                        cnt[\"S1p_fail\"] += 1\n                        if cnt[\"S1p_fail\"] == 1:\n                            cnt[\"S1p_first\"] = 0\n                            viol.append(f\"S1p-MEASURED\\t{line.strip()}\\tw={w} 1+F(G*)={1 + f_Gs - gd} F(G)={FG}\")\n                    if not okc:\n                        cnt[\"S1pc_fail\"] += 1\n\n    # ---- T1: Algorithm X -------------------------------------------------\n    if reduced and supp:\n        cnt[\"T1\"] += 1\n        X = 0\n        cur = list(adj)\n        while True:\n            comps_cur = components(cur)\n            nonbasic = [C for C in comps_cur if not is_basic_component(cur, C)]\n            if not nonbasic:\n                break\n            C = nonbasic[0]\n            _, chosen, _ = paper_choice(cur, C)\n            w = rng.choice(chosen)\n            X |= 1 << w\n            cur, _ = reduce(isolate(cur, w))\n        B = cur\n        if is_empty(B):\n            bad(\"T1empty\", f\"X={X:b}\")\n        if not is_reduced(B):\n            bad(\"T1reduced\", f\"X={X:b}\")\n        if not is_basic(B):\n            bad(\"T1basic\", f\"X={X:b}\")\n        if not X.bit_count() + fminus(B) <= fm:\n            bad(\"T1\", f\"X={X:b} |X|+fminus(B)={X.bit_count() + fminus(B)} fminus(G)={fm}\")\n        if X & ~supp:\n            bad(\"T1supp\", f\"X={X:b}\")\n        direct, _ = reduce(isolate_set(adj, X))\n        cnt[\"T1_direct\"] += 1\n        if direct != B:\n            cnt[\"T1_direct_differs\"] += 1\n        bump(\"T1_X\", X.bit_count())\n\n    # ---- C1, C2: the cut lemma --------------------------------------------\n    if heavy:\n        if n <= 7:\n            parts = range(0, 1 << (n - 1))     # V1 ∌ vertex n−1: each partition once\n        else:\n            parts = [rng.randrange(0, 1 << (n - 1)) for _ in range(C1_PARTITIONS)]\n        pwcache: dict[int, int] = {full: pw, 0: 0}\n\n        def pwS(S: int) -> int:\n            if S not in pwcache:\n                pwcache[S] = pw_induced(adj, S)\n            return pwcache[S]\n\n        for V1 in parts:\n            V2 = full & ~V1\n            b1 = sum(1 for v in bits(V1) if adj[v] & V2)\n            b2 = sum(1 for v in bits(V2) if adj[v] & V1)\n            bound = max(pwS(V1) + b1, pwS(V2) + b2, b1 + b2 - 1)\n            cnt[\"C1\"] += 1\n            if not pw <= bound:\n                bad(\"C1\", f\"V1={V1:b} pw={pw} bound={bound}\")\n            if pw <= max(pwS(V1) + b1, pwS(V2) + b2):\n                cnt[\"C1s_holds\"] += 1\n            bump(\"C1_slack\", bound - pw)\n        # C2: depth-2 bisection trees (random), budgets b_i = max boundary at level i\n        if n >= 4:\n            for _ in range(C2_TREES):\n                V1 = rng.randrange(0, 1 << (n - 1))\n                V2 = full & ~V1\n                lvl1 = max(sum(1 for v in bits(V1) if adj[v] & V2),\n                           sum(1 for v in bits(V2) if adj[v] & V1))\n                lvl2 = 0\n                leaves = []\n                for P in (V1, V2):\n                    pb = list(bits(P))\n                    sub = 0\n                    for v in pb:\n                        if rng.random() < 0.5:\n                            sub |= 1 << v\n                    Q1, Q2 = sub, P & ~sub\n                    lvl2 = max(lvl2,\n                               sum(1 for v in bits(Q1) if adj[v] & Q2),\n                               sum(1 for v in bits(Q2) if adj[v] & Q1))\n                    leaves += [pwS(Q1), pwS(Q2)]\n                bound = 2 * (lvl1 + lvl2) + max(leaves)\n                cnt[\"C2\"] += 1\n                if not pw <= bound:\n                    bad(\"C2\", f\"pw={pw} bound={bound}\")\n\n    return {\"n\": n, \"cnt\": cnt, \"mx\": mx, \"viol\": viol}\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# W1–W5 (main process)\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\ndef check_weights(N: int = 40) -> list[str]:\n    out = []\n    for d in range(4, N + 1):\n        assert d * g(d) == (d - 2) * g(d - 1) + g(d - 2) + 1, d          # W1\n    for d in range(0, N):\n        assert g(d + 1) >= g(d), d                                       # W2 (Lemma 8.3)\n    for d in range(3, N):\n        assert g_prime(d + 1) <= g_prime(d), d                           # W3 (Lemma 8.4)\n    for d in range(4, N + 1):\n        assert 1 - g(d) == (d - 1) * g_prime(d) + g_prime(d - 1), d      # W4 (property 6)\n    for d in range(0, N + 1):\n        assert 0 <= g(d) < 1, d                                          # W5a\n        assert 0 <= g_prime(d) <= Fraction(1, 6), d                      # W5b\n    for d in range(2, N + 1):\n        assert g_closed_form(d) == g(d), d                               # W5c (Lemma 8.1)\n    for d in range(5, N):                                                # property 5 (not used)\n        assert g(d + 1) / (d + 1) < g(d) / d, d\n    for d in range(5, N + 1):                                            # the g' recurrence\n        assert d * g_prime(d) == (d - 3) * g_prime(d - 1) + g_prime(d - 2), d\n    for d in range(4, N + 1):                                            # the sandwich\n        assert g_prime(d - 1) >= g_prime(d) >= g_prime(d - 1) / 3, d\n    for d in range(3, N + 1):                                            # coupled invariant\n        assert g(d - 1) <= g(d) <= (1 + g(d - 1)) / 2, d\n    out.append(f\"W1–W5 hold to n = {N} in exact rationals: recurrence (W1), g non-decreasing (W2), \"\n               f\"g' non-increasing from 3 (W3), property 6 (W4), 0 ≤ g < 1 and 0 ≤ g' ≤ 1/6 (W5), \"\n               f\"closed form (Lemma 8.1); also property 5, the g' recurrence n g'(n) = (n−3) g'(n−1) + g'(n−2) \"\n               f\"for n ≥ 5, the sandwich g'(n−1) ≥ g'(n) ≥ g'(n−1)/3 (n ≥ 4) and the coupled invariant \"\n               f\"g(n−1) ≤ g(n) ≤ (1 + g(n−1))/2 (n ≥ 3).\")\n    out.append(\"g(3..9) = \" + \", \".join(str(g(d)) for d in range(3, 10)))\n    out.append(\"g'(3..9) = \" + \", \".join(str(g_prime(d)) for d in range(3, 10)))\n    out.append(f\"A(1..6) = {[alternating_factorial(k) for k in range(1, 7)]}\")\n    return out\n\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# driver\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\ndef geng(n: int) -> list[str]:\n    return subprocess.run([\"nauty-geng\", \"-q\", str(n)], capture_output=True, text=True,\n                          check=True).stdout.splitlines()\n\n\ndef main() -> None:\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n    ap.add_argument(\"--max-n\", type=int, default=9)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--min-n\", type=int, default=1)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--workers\", type=int, default=8)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--no-stop\", action=\"store_true\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--log\", default=f\"{HERE}/check.log\")\n    a = ap.parse_args()\n\n    log = open(a.log, \"w\")\n\n    def say(s: str = \"\"):\n        print(s, flush=True)\n        log.write(s + \"\\n\")\n        log.flush()\n\n    say(f\"# item 02 brute-force check, {time.strftime('%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S UTC', time.gmtime())}, \"\n        f\"n = {a.min_n}..{a.max_n}, {a.workers} workers\")\n    for s in check_weights():\n        say(s)\n\n    violations: list[str] = []\n    per_n: dict[int, dict] = {}\n    t0 = time.time()\n    stop = False\n    with Pool(a.workers) as pool:\n        for n in range(a.min_n, a.max_n + 1):\n            lines = geng(n)\n            tn = time.time()\n            cnt: collections.Counter = collections.Counter()\n            mx: dict = {}\n            for res in pool.imap_unordered(one, list(enumerate(lines)), chunksize=64):\n                cnt.update(res[\"cnt\"])\n                for k, v in res[\"mx\"].items():\n                    if k not in mx or v > mx[k]:\n                        mx[k] = v\n                if res[\"viol\"]:\n                    hard = [v for v in res[\"viol\"] if not v.startswith(\"S1p-MEASURED\")]\n                    violations += res[\"viol\"]\n                    for v in res[\"viol\"]:\n                        say(\"VIOLATION \" + v if not v.startswith(\"S1p\") else \"MEASURED \" + v)\n                    if hard and not a.no_stop:\n                        stop = True\n                        break\n            per_n[n] = {\"cnt\": dict(cnt), \"mx\": {k: str(v) for k, v in mx.items()},\n                        \"seconds\": round(time.time() - tn, 1)}\n            say(f\"n={n}: {len(lines)} graphs in {time.time() - tn:.1f}s; \"\n                + \"; \".join(f\"{k}={v}\" for k, v in sorted(cnt.items()))\n                + \"; maxima \" + \", \".join(f\"{k}={v}\" for k, v in sorted(mx.items())))\n            if stop:\n                say(\"STOPPED on a violation\")\n                pool.terminate()\n                break\n    say(f\"total {time.time() - t0:.1f}s; violations (hard): \"\n        f\"{sum(1 for v in violations if not v.startswith('S1p'))}; \"\n        f\"S1′ measured failures: {sum(1 for v in violations if v.startswith('S1p'))}\")\n