rbed by the reflexive","+   closure, and \"`r(G)` is empty\" is `SPReduces G ⊥`.","+2. **The cut lemma has a stronger and simpler form, and it rests on two","+   existing lemmas.** The item's C1,","+   `pw(G) ≤ max(pw(G[V₁]) + |∂₁|, pw(G[V₂]) + |∂₂|, |∂₁| + |∂₂| − 1)`, is","+   implied by the *separator form*","+   **C1s: `pw(G) ≤ max(pw(G[V₁]), pw(G[V₂])) + min(|∂₁|, |∂₂|)`**, because","+   `∂₁` separates `V₁ ∖ ∂₁` from `V₂` (and symmetrically): delete `∂₁`","+   (`pathwidth_le_pathwidth_induce_add_card_compl`), the rest is a disjoint","+   union with no edge between (`pathwidth_induce_union_le_max`), and","+   `pw(G[V₁ ∖ ∂₁]) ≤ pw(G[V₁])` (`pathwidth_le_of_injective`). The three-term","+   bound follows from `max(a, b) + min(c, d) ≤ max(a + c, b + d)`. Checked:","+   C1s holds on all 71,967,757 partitions and is never above C1; it is tight","+   (`= pw`) on 9.5% of them. The iterated form C2 then carries the factor 1,","+   not 2: **C2s: `pw(G) ≤ Σ_i b_i + max_leaf pw`** with `b_i` bounding the","+   *smaller* boundary of each level-`i` split (checked on 2,306,072 random","+   depth-2 trees, with the item's factor-2 form beside it). Item 04 proves","+   C1s and derives C1 and both C2 forms; the note that Fomin–Høie's `n/6`","+   comes from one level and their Lemma 4, not from iterating, stands.","+3. **The floor on a non-cubic basic component is `5/6`, not on \"a","+   second-kind component\".** `K₄` is cubic *and* of the second kind","+   (`K₄ − v = K₃` reduces to empty) with `f⁻ = 1/2 < 5/6`. The true","+   statement is B1: *connected, every degree ≥ 3, not cubic ⇒ `f⁻ ≥ 5/6`*","+   (a vertex of degree ≥ 4 has four neighbours of degree ≥ 3, so","+   `f ≥ g(4) + 4 g(3) = 1`, and `g'(δ) ≤ 1/6`), basic or not; checked on all","+   89,943 such graphs. The assembly A1 does not need it: it needs only","+   `f⁻(C) ≥ 0` per component (checked on all 290,103 components), since the","+   `+1` of the second kind is carried explicitly in the budget.","+4. **P2's regular case is an equality and needs `Δ ≥ 4`.** Property 6 is","+   stated for `n ≥ 4` and fails at `n = 3` (`1 − g(3) = 5/6` against","+   `2 g'(3) + g'(2) = 1/3`), so for a `Δ`-regular reduced graph with `Δ ≥ 4`,","+   `f(G − w) = f(G) − 1 + g'(Δ − 1) − g'(Δ)` exactly (checked on all 501","+   such (graph, `w`) pairs); cubic graphs never reach the step (they are","+   basic), and there `f(G − w) = f(G) − 2/3`.","+5. **The step inequality is proved in the global-minimum form and the","+   per-component form follows.** The paper's equation (1) writes","+   `f⁻(G*) = f(G*) − g'(δ(G*))` with one global `δ`; with the design's","+   per-component `f⁻`, that is an inequality in the favourable direction,","+   `f⁻(G*) ≤ f(G*) − g'(δ(G*)) =: F(G*)` (every component's `g'(δ(C)) ≥ 0`","+   and one of them is `g'(δ(G*))`), and `f⁻(G) = F(G)` for `G` connected on","+   its support. So item 07 proves **S1: `1 + F(G*) ≤ F(G)`** and gets","+   `1 + f⁻(G*) ≤ f⁻(G)` as a corollary. Both were checked (137,573 pairs).","+6. **Theorem 3.2 needs `G ≠ ⊥`** in the Lean form, since \"every degree 0 or","+   ≥ 3\" admits the edgeless graph, for which no non-empty basic reduct","+   exists. And **no confluence fact is needed anywhere**: \"not basic\" is","+   `∀ v, ¬ SPReduces (G − v) ⊥` (the second-kind clause is existential over","+   reduction sequences), so `G* ≠ ⊥` for *the* reduct the induction supplies","+   is immediate; the commutation lemma R3/R4 does the rest, as the plan","+   said.","+","+### 2.2 The statements","+","+Numbered as items 03–09 will prove them; `G − w` is `isolate`, `δ(H)` the","+minimum degree over the support (0 if empty), `F(H) = f(H) − g'(δ(H))`,","+`supp` the vertices of positive degree. The paper's location and the check","+count are given; the Lean name, file and the existing lemma each rests on are","+in §2.6.","+","+| # | statement | hypotheses | paper | checked on |","+|---|---|---|---|---|","+| W1 | `n g(n) = (n − 2) g(n − 1) + g(n − 2) + 1` | `n ≥ 4` | p. 6 | `n ≤ 40` exact |","+| W2 | `g(n) ≤ g(n + 1)` (`g` non-decreasing) | all `n` | Lemma 8.3 | `n ≤ 40` |","+| W3 | `g'(n + 1) ≤ g'(n)` | `n ≥ 3` | Lemma 8.4 | `n ≤ 40` |","+| W4 | `1 − g(n) = (n − 1) g'(n) + g'(n − 1)` | `n ≥ 4` | property 6 | `n ≤ 40` |","+| W5 | `0 ≤ g(n) < 1`; `0 ≤ g'(n) ≤ 1/6`; `g'(n) ≤ g(n)` | all `n` | p. 7 | `n ≤ 40` |","+| W5c | closed form `g(n) = (7/2) A(n)/n! + (3/2)(−1)ⁿ/n! − 5/2` (optional) | `n ≥ 2` | Lemma 8.1 | `n ≤ 40` |","+| C1s | `pw(G) ≤ max(pw(G[V₁]), pw(G[V₂])) + min(|∂₁|, |∂₂|)` | any partition | — (ours; §2.1 (2)) | 71,967,757 partitions, every graph to 9 |","+| C1 | `pw(G) ≤ max(pw(G[V₁]) + |∂₁|, pw(G[V₂]) + |∂₂|, |∂₁| + |∂₂| − 1)` | any partition | — (the item's form; Fomin–Høie's `P₁, P₂, P₃` shape) | the same |","+| C2s / C2 | depth-`h` bisection with per-level budgets `b_i` on the smaller (C2s) or larger (C2) boundary: `pw(G) ≤ Σ b_i + max_leaf pw`, resp. `≤ 2 Σ b_i + max_leaf pw` | — | — | 2,306,072 random depth-2 trees |","+| P1 | `f(G − w) = f(G) − g(d(w)) − Σ_{v ∈ N(w)} g'(d(v))` | none | (2)–(3) | 2,579,255 (graph, `w`) |","+| P2 | `f(G − w) ≤ f(G) − 1` | every degree 0 or ≥ 3; `d(w) = Δ ≥ 4`; some neighbour of degree `≤ Δ − 1` | p. 10 | 163,265 |","+| P2r | `f(G − w) = f(G) − 1 + g'(Δ − 1) − g'(Δ)` | `Δ`-regular on the support, `Δ ≥ 4` | p. 11 | 501 |","+| R1 | one step removes at least one edge (so `SPReduces` terminates and a reduced reduct exists) | step at degree 1 or 2 | p. 8 | 393,156 steps |","+| R2 | one step raises no degree: `d_{H'}(u) ≤ d_H(u)` for every `u`; hence `f(H') ≤ f(H)`, and a vertex of degree `d` isolated by the step costs `f(H) − f(H') ≥ g(d)` | — | p. 10 (\"`v` is reduced away\") | 393,156 |","+| R3 | `SPStep H H'` at `v`, `w ≠ v` ⇒ `H' − w = H − w`, or `SPStep (H − w) (H' − w)` at `v` | — | replaces Lemma 3.1 | 3,115,987 (graph, step, `w`): 95,300 zero-step, 3,020,687 one-step |","+| R4 | lift of R3 to `SPReduces` and to a finset `X` disjoint from the acted vertices | — | Lemma 3.1 | by induction from R3 (R3 is the whole content; not separately swept) |","+| R5 | a step at `v` acts inside the component of `v`: `step(G|C ⊔ G|Cᶜ, v) = step(G|C, v) ⊔ G|Cᶜ` | `v ∈ C` | p. 9 (disconnected case) | 8,350 |","+| R6 | `pw(H) ≤ pw(H') + 1` for one step (optional; not what A1 needs) | — | plan §0.3 | 393,156; the drop is 0 or 1 |","+| S0 | `G*` a reduced reduct of `G' = G − w`, `d_{G'}(v) = d ≥ 3` ⇒ `f(G') − f(G*) + g'(δ(G*)) ≥ g'(d)` | none beyond those | p. 10, the `j₄` lemma | 1,093,524 |","+| SJ | `1 + f(G') = f(G) − j₁ − j₂ − j₃` | every degree 0 or ≥ 3, `d(w) = Δ ≥ 4` | (2)–(4) | 157,324 |","+| S1 | `1 + F(G*) ≤ F(G)` (hence `1 + f⁻(G*) ≤ f⁻(G)`) | `G` connected on its support, every degree 0 or ≥ 3, not basic; `w` of maximum degree whose lowest-degree neighbour has the smallest degree; `G*` any reduced reduct of `G − w` | p. 9–12, equation (1) | 137,573 (graph, `w`, reduct), reducts canonical and random |","+| S1′ | the same for *every* maximum-degree `w` | — | — | **false**: 663 of 157,324 fail (§2.4) |","+| T1 | `∃ X ⊆ supp G, B`: `SPReduces (G − X) B`, `B ≠ ⊥`, `B` reduced and basic, `|X| + f⁻(B) ≤ f⁻(G)` | every degree 0 or ≥ 3, `G ≠ ⊥` | Theorem 3.2, Algorithm X | 89,972 reduced non-empty graphs; also `r(G − X) = B` on all |","+| B1 | `f⁻(C) ≥ 0` for every component; additivity `f⁻(G) = Σ_C f⁻(G|C)`; connected cubic ⇒ `f⁻ = N/6 − 1/6`; connected, every degree ≥ 3, not cubic ⇒ `f⁻ ≥ 5/6` | — | p. 7, p. 19 | 290,103 components; 288,266 graphs; 24 cubic; 89,943 non-cubic |","+| A1 | `pw(G) ≤ f⁻(G) + τ(n) + 2ρ(n) + 1` under `CubicPathwidthBound τ`, `ReductionPathwidthBound ρ`, `τ, ρ` monotone | every degree 0 or ≥ 3 | Lemma 5.1 | the budget it needs at `n ≤ 9`: §2.5 |","+| A2 | `pw(G) ≤ Σ_v g(d_{r(G)}(v)) + τ(n) + 3ρ(n) + 1 ≤ Σ_v g(d_G(v)) + …` | any `G` | Corollary 5.2 | §2.5 |","+","+### 2.3 The counts","+","+| `n` | graphs | C1/C1s partitions | C1s tight | R3 triples | reduction orders | S1 pairs | S1′ pairs (fail) | non-basic | T1 graphs | `pw − f⁻` max (reduced) | `pw − main` max | `pw(G) − pw(r(G))` max (count at max) |","+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|","+| 1–3 | 7 | 21 | 19 | 18 | 800 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 2 | 2 (1) |","+| 4 | 11 | 88 | 55 | 84 | 1,800 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 1 | 5/2 (`K₄`) | 7/3 | 2 (4) |","+| 5 | 34 | 544 | 247 | 376 | 5,800 | 5 | 5 (0) | 1 | 4 | 5/2 | 7/3 | 2 (17) |","+| 6 | 156 | 4,992 | 1,503 | 2,075 | 26,400 | 31 | 31 (0) | 8 | 23 | 5/2 | 3 | 3 (1) |","+| 7 | 1,044 | 66,816 | 13,235 | 14,514 | 174,000 | 242 | 261 (2) | 100 | 173 | 5/2 | 3 | 3 (8) |","+| 8 | 12,346 | 1,580,288 | 207,427 | 158,200 | 1,916,400 | 4,240 | 4,718 (42) | 2,234 | 2,763 | 17/6 (the two cubic graphs of pw 4) | 3 | 3 (114) |","+| 9 | 274,668 | 70,315,008 | 6,617,710 | 2,940,720 | 37,531,800 | 133,055 | 152,309 (619) | 82,419 | 87,008 | 17/6 | 3 | 3 (1,258) |","+| all | 288,266 | 71,967,757 | 6,840,196 | 3,115,987 | 39,657,000 | 137,573 | 157,324 (663) | 84,762 | 89,972 | 17/6 | 3 | 3 (1,381) |","+","+Every other statement's count is in §2.2; every check printed its count and","+no violation line was written (`violations.txt` holds only the 350 S1′","+measurement lines, one per failing graph).","+","+### 2.4 The two measurements","+","+**S1′ is false; the paper's tie-break is necessary.** Among the 157,324","+(connected non-basic graph, maximum-degree `w`, reduct) triples, 663 — on 350","+graphs, the first at 7 vertices — violate `1 + F(G*) ≤ F(G)`; none of the","+137,573 with the paper's `w` does. **Every one of the 350 has all neighbours","+of `w` at the maximum degree `Δ` while `G` is not regular** (`Δ = 5` on 298,","+6 on 50, 7 on 2), and the violation is exactly `g'(Δ − 1) − g'(Δ)`","+(`1/15`, `1/45`, `2/105`): the paper's term `j₁ = g'(d(v₁)) − g'(Δ − 1)` is","+negative for such a `w`, the regular-case rescue (`G'` has a vertex of degree","+`Δ − 1`, so `j₄ ≥ g'(Δ − 1)`) is what the proof uses when *every* vertex has","+degree `Δ`, and for a non-regular `G` the paper's rule picks a `w` with a","+lower-degree neighbour instead, which makes `j₁ ≥ 0`. The smallest example","+is `F]~vo` (7 vertices, degrees 5,5,5,5,5,4,5: `K₇` minus a path of two","+edges): vertices 4 and 6 have five neighbours of degree 5, and deleting","+either leaves a 4-regular graph with `1 + F(G*) = 17/6 > F(G) = 83/30`; the","+four vertices adjacent to the degree-4 vertex satisfy the inequality with","+equality. So **item 07 must choose `w` by the two-key rule** — maximum","+degree, then the smallest lowest-neighbour degree — and the simple","+`Finset.exists_max_image` over the degree alone does not suffice;","+`tests/test_edwards_mcdermid.py::test_paper_choice_tie_break_is_needed`","+pins the example.","+","+**The reduct is unique on every graph to 9 vertices.** 200 maximal","+reduction sequences in uniformly random order on each of the 198,285 graphs","+with a step (39,657,000 sequences) all reached the canonical reduct, and on","+all 89,972 Theorem 3.2 instances the direct `r(G − X)` equals the graph","+Algorithm X ends with. This is the paper's \"(the resulting graph `r(G)` is in","+fact unique)\" measured, not proved; the Lean design does not use it (§2.1 (6)).","+","+### 2.5 The budgets the record needs at `n ≤ 9`, and the shape of (H3)","+","+`pw − f⁻` over reduced graphs has maximum `5/2` at `n = 4–7` (`K₄`: pw 3,","+`f⁻ = 1/2`) and `17/6` at `n = 8–9` (the two cubic graphs on 8 vertices of","+pathwidth 4, `f⁻ = 7/6`); `pw − Σ_{r(G)} g` over all graphs has maximum 3","+from `n = 6` on, attained first by the series-parallel graph `EElw` (a","+triangle with each edge subdivided once, pathwidth 3, main term 0) and at","+`n = 8` by 114 graphs, all reducing to empty. These are the values","+`τ(n) + 2ρ(n) + 1` and `τ(n) + 3ρ(n) + 1` must reach at these sizes, nothing","+more; they match §1.3's `B(n)` (3.333 at `n ≤ 10`, the Petersen graph).","+","+`pw(G) − pw(r(G))` is 0 on 273,776 graphs, 1 on 3,210, 2 on 9,899 and","+**3 on 1,381** (first at `n = 6`, `EElw` again: series-parallel with","+pathwidth 3). The item expected at most 2; the shape of (H3) at these sizes","+is 3, consistent with `O(log n)` (the complete ternary tree of height 3 has 40","+vertices and pathwidth 3, but subdivided triangles get there at 6) and","+nothing about its constant. The gap is never negative (`r(G)` is a minor of","+`G`), and one step never costs more than one (R6, drop 0 or 1 on all 393,156","+steps).","+","+**Kill verdict: not met** for every deterministic statement (W1–W5, C1–C2,","+P1–P2, R1–R6, S0–S1, SJ, T1, B1); the two measurements are findings (S1′","+false; reduct unique to 9), as the item provided for.","+","+**What this does not claim.** Anything for `n > 9` (the checks are","+exhaustive to 9 and nothing else); that the reduct is unique in general","+(measured to 9; the design does not need it); that (H1) or (H3) hold or what","+their constants are (only the shape `pw(H) − pw(r(H)) ≤ 3` to 9 vertices is","+measured); that C1s is new (it is the standard separator argument; \"we found","+no prior statement\" of the item's three-term form is not claimed either,","+since Fomin–Høie's proof has that shape); that S1′ fails beyond the pattern","+seen (every failure to 9 has all neighbours at degree `Δ`; no other pattern","+was looked for).","+","+### 2.6 The Lean-ready list for items 03–09","+","+Every graph is a `SimpleGraph V` on one finite vertex type with decidable","+equality and adjacency; `G − w` is `G.isolate w` (`Minor.lean`), `G − X` the","+fold of `isolate` over `X : Finset V`; `supp G` is the finset of vertices of","+positive degree; \"`G` is reduced\" (`IsSPReduced G`) is `∀ v, G.degree v = 0 ∨ 3 ≤ G.degree v`.","+Hypotheses are written as they should appear in the Lean statement; the last","+column is the existing lemma or the earlier item each rests on.","+","+**`DegreeBound/Weights.lean` (item 03)** — `g : ℕ → ℚ`, `g' n = g n − g (n − 1)`.","+","+| name | statement | rests on |","+|---|---|---|","+| `g_zero, g_one, g_two, g_three` | `g 0 = g 1 = g 2 = 0`, `g 3 = 1/6` | definition |","+| `g_recurrence` (W1) | `4 ≤ n → n * g n = (n − 2) * g (n − 1) + g (n − 2) + 1` | definition (well-founded recursion) |","+| `g_table` | `g 4 = 1/3`, `g 5 = 13/30`, `g 6 = 23/45`, `g 7 = 359/630`, `g 8 = 1553/2520`; `g' 3 = g' 4 = 1/6`, `g' 5 = 1/10` | `norm_num` on the recurrence |","+| `g_monotone` (W2, Lemma 8.3) | `Monotone g` | the coupled invariant `g (n−1) ≤ g n ≤ (1 + g (n−1))/2` by induction |","+| `g'_recurrence` | `5 ≤ n → n * g' n = (n − 3) * g' (n − 1) + g' (n − 2)` | W1 twice |","+| `g'_antitone_of_three_le` (W3, Lemma 8.4) | `3 ≤ m → m ≤ n → g' n ≤ g' m` | the sandwich `g' (n−1) ≥ g' n ≥ g' (n−1)/3` by induction from `g'_recurrence` |","+| `one_sub_g_eq` (W4, property 6) | `4 ≤ n → 1 − g n = (n − 1) * g' n + g' (n − 1)` | W1 rearranged |","+| `g_nonneg, g_lt_one, g'_nonneg, g'_le_sixth` (W5) | `0 ≤ g n`, `g n < 1`, `0 ≤ g' n`, `g' n ≤ 1/6` | W2, W3, the coupled invariant |","+| `g'_le_g` | `g' n ≤ g n` | `g_nonneg` at `n − 1` (used by S0) |","+| `g_closed_form` (Lemma 8.1, optional) | `2 ≤ n → g n = (7/2) A n / n! + (3/2) (−1)^n / n! − 5/2` with `A` the alternating factorial | induction; not needed downstream |","+","+**`DegreeBound/CutLemma.lean` (item 04)** — `boundary G S := S.filter (fun v => ∃ u, u ∉ S ∧ G.Adj v u)`.","+","+| name | statement | rests on |","+|---|---|---|","+| `pathwidth_le_max_add_min_boundary` (C1s) | `pathwidth G ≤ max (pathwidth (G.induce ↑S)) (pathwidth (G.induce ↑Sᶜ)) + min |∂S| |∂Sᶜ|` | `pathwidth_le_pathwidth_induce_add_card_compl` with the complement `∂S`; `pathwidth_induce_union_le_max` on `S ∖ ∂S` and `Sᶜ` (no edge between them); `pathwidth_le_of_injective` for `G[S ∖ ∂S] ≤ G[S]` |","+| `pathwidth_le_cut` (C1) | `pathwidth G ≤ max (max (pathwidth G[S] + |∂S|) (pathwidth G[Sᶜ] + |∂Sᶜ|)) (|∂S| + |∂Sᶜ| − 1)` | C1s and `max a b + min c d ≤ max (a + c) (b + d)` |","+| `BisectionTree G S bs k` | `BisectionTree S [] k := pathwidth G[S] ≤ k`; `BisectionTree S (b :: bs) k := ∃ S₁ S₂, S₁ ∪ S₂