{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CgdE8WtXhDnZ2XmYyGrQr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Item 02 is done. Nine items remain unchecked, so no `LOOP_COMPLETE` line.\n\n**What was done.** Every intermediate statement of the Edwards–McDermid chain was written out in the plan's Lean design and checked on every graph on 1 to 9 vertices (288,266 graphs, 335 s). Nothing was sampled: the cut lemma was checked on every partition of every graph, the commutation lemma on every (graph, step, w) triple, the reduct's uniqueness on 200 random orders per graph, and S1′ on every maximum-degree vertex.\n\n**Kill verdict: not met.** Zero violations of W1–W5, C1, C2, P1, P2, R1, R2, R3, R5, R6, S0, S1, SJ, T1 and B1. The loop's premise for the Lean items stands.\n\n**Two findings, both of the kind the item allowed for.**\n- **S1′ is false.** Taking any maximum-degree vertex fails on 350 graphs from 7 vertices up, every time with all neighbours at the maximum degree in a non-regular graph. The paper's two-key rule never fails. Item 07 must keep the tie-break. The smallest example is pinned by a test.\n- **The reduct is unique** on every graph to 9 vertices. The Lean design does not need this and no confluence fact is needed anywhere in the chain.\n\n**Six corrections to the design and the item's wording**, in report §2.1. The most useful one: the cut lemma has a stronger separator form, the maximum of the two sides' pathwidths plus the *smaller* boundary, which rests on three existing lemmas and implies the item's three-term form. The iterated form then carries factor 1, not 2. The others: the step relation is defined at degrees 1 and 2 only, the 5/6 floor is for non-cubic components, P2's regular case is an equality needing Δ ≥ 4, S1 is proved in global-minimum form, and Theorem 3.2 needs a non-empty graph.\n\n**Measured shapes.** The reduction gap `pw(G) − pw(r(G))` reaches 3 at 6 vertices, not the expected 2. The budgets the record needs at these sizes peak at 17/6 and 3.\n\n**Files.** Report §2 with the Lean-ready list for items 03–09 in `reports/edwards_mcdermid.md`. Script, log, violations and summary under `reports/scratch/edwards_mcdermid/02_lemmas/`. Helpers added to `learning/edwards_mcdermid.py` with 9 new tests. Gate passed: Lean build ok, zero sorry and axiom, both pytest suites green, paper check ok. PROGRESS.md and iterations.md updated. Nothing committed, nothing under `solutions/` touched.\n\n**Next.** Item 03, the weights file in Lean, with both induction invariants already checked to n = 40 in exact rationals."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":290,"cache_read_input_tokens":232278,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":290,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":790,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8b20c5ed-4e93-4acb-9f13-261a84c24494","uuid":"f583a49d-e3ec-4dc8-93b0-fab644096b54","timestamp":"2026-11-02T01:23:38.990Z","request_id":"req_011CgdE8WUioq8paKuvxYXHn"}
